nce if you need to and repeat."], [135.2, "Or you can pause after all of the story and try to tell the entire story."], [140.0, "Beginning with the phrase."], [141.5, "20 years ago."], [144.2, "All right, let's jump to the future now."], [145.9, "I have a new movie idea."], [147.1, "It's a science fiction movie."], [149.1, "And it's going to be in 2050."], [152.3, "And I'm going to tell you about my movie idea."], [154.2, "Here we go."], [154.6, "In the year 2050, there will be a guy named Bob."], [160.8, "Bob will be a newlywed."], [163.0, "He and his wife will have been married only two months."], [167.7, "Unfortunately, Bob will be an authoritarian husband."], [170.8, "Every day he will tell Kathy, cook my food, clean this house, serve me, woman!"], [176.8, "Bob will feel he is entitled to be served like a king by his wife."], [181.6, "Now, Kathy will be a very sweet wife."], [185.7, "She's going to be very sensitive, and she's going to emote strongly."], [190.5, "She'll always show her true feelings."], [193.8, "Kathy will have had a strict upbringing."], [197.3, "Her mom will have told her to always obey her husband."], [201.2, "Since she has strong, she will have strong moral fiber."], [205.1, "Kathy will try to do what her mom taught."], [207.8, "But every day she will become more sad because of Bob."], [213.4, "Finally, she's gonna yell at him with righteous indignation."], [216.8, "Shut up you pig!"], [218.0, "I want a divorce."], [220.1, "Bob is gonna be so shocked he will have a heart attack and then he's gonna die."], [225.9, "After that, nobody's going to mourn him."], [229.0, "Nobody will mourn Bob."], [231.5, "Kathy will take his life insurance money and then she's gonna be very happy."], [235.9, "She will be very happy because she'll be free and she'll be rich."], [241.0, "All right."], [242.2, "Very good."], [243.5, "So that obviously is using the future, right?"], [245.3, "We're talking about the year 2050."], [247.9, "Now you notice I sound like I made a mistake there, but actually I started using the present tense and then I switched to using future."], [256.2, "That's okay."], [257.1, "Actually in English, sometimes when we talk about the future, sometimes we use the present tense."], [263.2, "So, actually, in many cases, you can use both."], [268.1, "I changed because I wanted to keep using the future tense only, so just to help you remember it."], [274.0, "But in fact, when you talk about the future, you can sometimes use the present tense."], [279.1, "So don't let that confuse you."], [281.7, "All right."], [282.5, "Now let's tell it one more time."], [284.6, "I'm going to begin the story with the phrase, since two months ago."], [289.9, "Okay?"], [291.2, "Since two months ago."], [292.9, "Starting two months ago."], [294.4, "Okay."], [295.4, "Since two months ago, there has been a couple named Bob and Kathy who are newlyweds."], [304.5, "Unfortunately, Bob has been an authoritarian husband during these two months."], [311.1, "Every day he has yelled at Kathy, cook my food."], [315.0, "Clean this house."], [316.4, "Serve me, woman.\""], [318.0, "Now during this time, this two months."], [320.2, "Bob has felt he is entitled to be served like a king by his wife."], [325.2, "Now Kathy, his wife, she's a very sweet woman."], [329.1, "She's very sensitive and she has always emoted strongly."], [334.1, "She has always showed her true feelings to Bob."], [338.5, "Kathy, in the past, had a strict upbringing."], [341.4, "Her mom told her to always obey her future husband."], [346.3, "Now since she has strong moral fiber."], [349.1, "And during this two months she has had strong moral fiber."], [353.5, "Kathy has tried to do what her mom taught her."], [356.9, "But every day she has become more sad because of Bob."], [362.0, "Finally one day she's sick of it."], [365.6, "Finally one day she yells at him."], [368.9, "And, she yells at him with righteous indignation."], [371.7, "She says, shut up you pig, I want a divorce."], [375.1, "Well, Bob is so shocked, he has a heart attack and dies."], [378.8, "But after he's dead, nobody mourns."], [382.9, "Kathy takes his life insurance money and is now very happy."], [388.5, "Okay, you'll notice in that one, I use have had, have gone, right, in the beginning."], [393.6, "Starting, whenever I'm talking about during the last two months."], [397.9, "Since two months ago."], [399.5, "It means starting two months ago and continuing all up until now."], [405.5, "Anytime I'm talking about something that has continued."], [408.6, "That started two months ago and has continued until now, I'm using have gone, have had, right?"], [415.3, "But then I change to the present tense."], [418.2, "I say finally one day, okay?"], [421.8, "Now I change to the present tense."], [423.7, "I could change to the past tense."], [425.5, "I could have said finally one day she yelled at him, shut up you pig."], [430.9, "And then Bob was so shocked..."], [432.7, "I could tell the rest of the story, the end of the story, in the past tense,"], [437.9, "if I say that happened in the past."], [441.2, "I decided to tell it in the present tense, meaning it's, I started two months ago."], [447.0, "I come up until now, the end of the story is told in the present tense."], [451.9, "The end of the story is happening recently."], [456.1, "But the beginning of the story, I'm talking about what has happened during this whole time, during a period that started in the past two months ago and has continued until recently."], [470.6, "Okay, again, don't think too much about the grammar terms."], [474.6, "You don't need to know present perfect, past perfect, that's not important."], [479.2, "What I want you to do is listen many times to each version."], [482.8, "Pause, go back, listen again."], [485.1, "Then try to maybe repeat or copy individual sentences."], [490.2, "Then try to repeat and copy telling all of the story, all of the version using the beginning phrases."], [496.0, "20 years ago is version number one, version number two in 2050."], [503.2, "And version number three since two months ago."], [507.7, "All right, good luck."], [509.0, "See you next time."], [509.7, "Bye-bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.6, "Okay, welcome to the commentary for the Emotionally Intelligent Husbands article."], [6.4, "I'll just chat about why I chose this and what it means to me."], [10.6, "I chose this, I guess."], [12.3, "Because I myself am hoping to improve my relationship with Tomoe and always trying to be better."], [22.0, "And this is from a very interesting book by Dr. John Gottman."], [27.3, "I'm trying to remember the name of the book exactly."], [28.7, "The seven principles of good marriage, something like that."], [32.6, "Anyway, Gottman's interesting, Dr. John Gottman."], [36.2, "He's a researcher."], [37.4, "He does research on marriages."], [39.9, "So his book is based not just on his opinion or experience, but also on research."], [47.2, "And what they do is they, he and his group, research marriages."], [51.0, "And they try to figure out what causes marriages to succeed and what causes them to fail."], [60.9, "And his definition of success and failure are important."], [65.7, "Success means that both partners report, say, they are very happy with the relationship."], [73.6, "So that's success."], [74.9, "And failure means, number one, of course, divorce."], [77.4, "Worse, but it also means, number two."], [80.4, "That one or both partners."], [83.0, "Husband wife, girlfriend and boyfriend, are very unhappy."], [86.7, "So that's failure."], [87.4, "So some people remain married, but they're not happy."], [90.2, "So that's considered a failure by Dr. Gottman in his research."], [94.3, "So they find these groups of marriages, these two kinds of marriages, and then they study these people."], [100.3, "It's quite interesting, they study them in very close detail."], [103.6, "Of course, they interview them and get lots of information."], [107.4, "But they do much more than that."], [108.9, "They bring them in to their research, I don't know if you want to call it a lab office maybe."], [114.9, "They bring them into their office and then many times, and they have them discuss different topics."], [121.8, "And sometimes they argue, sometimes they agree, whatever."], [125.0, "But they have the husband and wife talk about topics."], [127.4, "While they're talking, they measure their heart rate and their sweat glands, how much they're sweating."], [135.3, "They also videotape them very closely, especially their faces, their emotions."], [140.8, "And after these videotaped conversations, after this research, they go back."], [147.7, "They watch the videotape step by step, like each frame."], [152.4, "When they do it, when they watch it very slow like that,"], [156.4, "they can see very quick gestures."], [159.4, "Very quick emotions on the face."], [162.6, "When you're just looking at normal speed, you don't see them."], [165.6, "But when you look at a video and you go slow, slow motion, you can see really quickly some quick emotion show on the face."], [174.5, "So anyway, they have all this information, all this data about heart rate and all these videotapes."], [180.7, "And then they study them very carefully and they identify."], [183.9, "You know, what are the things that are the same for the successful marriages, the successful couples, and what are the things that are the same for the failing couples, or the divorced couples, or the ones that are probably going to be divorced."], [199.1, "And from this research, he has identified different key traits."], [205.4, "Key things you must do for your marriage to be successful."], [210.4, "And this article is one of them, and of course it's focused mostly on the husband."], [215.3, "Other things are focused on the wife or focused on both of them, but for my own purpose, I'm of course worried more about what I can do myself."], [224.2, "So this is focused on the husband, and one key trait is that the husbands need to be emotionally intelligent."], [230.7, "It means they have to learn how to deal with their emotions in a healthy way."], [237.7, "And this has two sides."], [239.3, "One side is they have to be able to understand and respect other people's emotions."], [245.7, "Of course, their wife's feelings."], [247.6, "The husband needs to be able to understand and respect his wife's feelings, but also his children's feelings and his friends' feelings, just in general."], [255.6, "He has to know how to understand and identify and talk about other people's feelings."], [262.3, "And to be sensitive to those feelings, and to care about those feelings."], [265.8, "And then the other side of it, he has to be able to identify and understand and communicate his own feelings."], [273.0, "So he's got to be able to talk about his own feelings, and not just anger."], [276.8, "Not just, I'm pissed off, but also when he's sad and other things."], [280.6, "He has to be able to clearly understand those feelings, handle them, and communicate them in a positive way, in a respectful way."], [290.2, "And a lot of this has to do with what he calls accepting influence from his wife."], [297.0, "This is what Dr. Gottman says, accepting influence is a key part of emotional intelligence."], [303.1, "What does that mean?"], [303.8, "Well, what it really means practically, simply, is that the husband has to share power with his wife."], [312.3, "He influences his wife, of course, he has some."], [315.9, "Not controls a bad word."], [318.1, "He affects his wife, he changes his wife somewhat, but he also has to be willing to be changed."], [325.1, "He has to be willing, he has to let his wife change him."], [328.9, "He has to accept her power, he has to accept her influence also."], [332.5, "It has to be both ways."], [335.2, "So accepting influence, sharing power, is very important for marriages, especially now."], [341.6, "In most countries, society is changing."], [344.2, "Women are getting more power."], [346.2, "Those old ideas from the 1950s, man is in control, the man is the leader."], [353.2, "The man says what is done and the woman does it."], [357.1, "Those ideas don't work anymore."], [358.6, "They certainly don't work in America or Europe, as we know, or Latin America."], [363.6, "And in Asia, I know this is also changing quite a lot, and really this doesn't work in Asia anymore either, simply because women will not tolerate it anymore, right?"], [374.2, "They're sick of it, and they're not gonna put up with this anymore."], [378.1, "It doesn't matter what men like or don't like, or want or don't want; the women will not accept this anymore."], [384.4, "In my opinion, that's good."], [385.9, "So I'm quite happy about that, I think it's a good thing."], [390.5, "But it's an adjustment, and he's right about that."], [393.4, "In the past men."], [394.9, "Especially older generation."], [398.1, "My father's generation, my grandfather's generation."], [401.2, "They did have that entitlement, you know, they had that feeling that naturally men should be the leader, naturally men should have the power, or more power."], [410.8, "And naturally women should be weaker."], [412.6, "They have this strong idea, society taught them that."], [415.8, "Their own family taught them that, so it's hard for them to change."], [420.0, "Some of them have a difficult time changing."], [423.9, "They feel they're losing that entitlement, and some of them do respond with righteous indignation."], [429.7, "They do respond with anger."], [431.9, "Now to be fair, some of them do not."], [433.7, "You know, actually my own father, I've seen him change quite a bit."], [438.5, "And I've known plenty of older men."], [440.5, "In my father's age."], [442.1, "In fact, my grandfather, my mother's father, was not like that at all."], [447.1, "He very much shared power with my grandmother."], [450.7, "In fact, I would say my grandmother was the stronger one in their relationship."], [455.9, "So, you know, we have to be careful."], [458.2, "These are general trends in societies, but they're not true of every single person."], [463.6, "However, I think I think Dr. Gottman is absolutely correct."], [466.9, "That in general."], [468.3, "In modern societies especially."], [472.1, "Things have changed."], [473.7, "And to have a successful marriage, as a husband, you must give up your power."], [479.6, "It doesn't mean you're weak, it means you share power."], [482.3, "It means you're strong about your own ideas and opinions, but you also respect your wife's strength, and you let her, and you want her to be strong, and you want her to express her opinions and that it's a partnership, an equal partnership."], [497.6, "I think Dr. Gottman is definitely right about that."], [501.8, "If you do this, it creates healthier relationships."], [505.5, "I think a lot of men."], [507.3, "These old-fashioned men, they feel threatened, they're afraid of this."], [511.7, "But actually I have found in my own life it's quite positive."], [516.3, "It's a lot less stressful when you share power with someone else, when you're a partner."], [521.2, "If you have all the power, it seems like it's great, you can, oh, clean my room."], [526.7, "But, on the other hand, you also have all the responsibility."], [531.1, "And that's very stressful."], [533.4, "Another thing, I think, from the man's point of view."], [537.7, "A woman who serves you who's not equal, let's face it, it's boring."], [541.6, "It's extremely boring."], [543.3, "You know, I know for my own part, I don't want a servant."], [546.5, "I want a partner, I want an equal partner."], [548.3, "I want someone who has strong opinions and strong ideas, who's very intelligent, who's very confident."], [554.1, "I can learn from her."], [556.4, "And hopefully, I hope, she learns from me, too."], [560.4, "So anyway, it's interesting because I read this article, we studied this article in my class here in San Francisco."], [569.0, "And I was a little shocked, to be honest."], [572.2, "About the reaction, several, I guess I have to say several of the Asian students."], [578.9, "Especially the men, not surprisingly."], [581.9, "Disagreed strongly with this article."], [585.0, "They didn't like this idea, they thought the man must be the boss and the woman naturally must follow him, and that is the way the world is supposed to work, or I don't know, God says this is true, or society."], [600.2, "Or whatever, they still had a very strong idea about this."], [602.9, "And to be fair, there was actually at least one Asian woman who thought the same thing, who thought a woman should follow men."], [612.2, "Now for an American, and I'm sure for most Europeans, it was quite a shock."], [617.4, "I couldn't believe they were saying that."], [619.9, "But you know, I should not have been surprised I've lived in Asia."], [623.3, "However, I have lived in Asia, and I also know that the women in Asia are changing, and that these men may not like these changes."], [630.5, "However, they can't stop it."], [633.3, "So even if you don't like it, I think you have no choice."], [637.1, "You have to adjust if you want to have a marriage because, you know, to be really direct."], [644.2, "If you have this old idea and you marry a woman today in modern life."], [649.7, "If you act like this, she's probably going to divorce you."], [653.9, "You can try to be the big strong boss."], [656.2, "But you know, you're probably fine that after a few years or sooner, she's just going to divorce you."], [662.4, "So if you really do want a happy family and a happy life, I think you've got to change."], [669.2, "And I think that's as true in Japan and Korea and Taiwan and China and Thailand as it is in Europe and America and Latin America."], [680.1, "I think it's true all over the world, really."], [684.2, "Now, from a woman's point of view, of course."], [688.1, "I think this is a very, very positive trend."], [691.0, "That women should be equal."], [693.8, "They're equally intelligent, equally smart, equally strong."], [698.0, "Maybe not physically in terms of lifting weights, but it's not important in modern society anymore."], [703.3, "So anyway, okay, that's all."], [706.3, "I will see you next time."], [708.0, "I hope you enjoy this lesson."], [709.9, "Please go to the forums."], [712.0, "Write your opinions about the role."], [715.3, "The proper role for husbands and wives in relationships."], [719.2, "Do you agree with my opinions here?"], [722.4, "Do you agree with Dr. Gottman's opinions and his research?"], [726.4, "I don't mind."], [727.0, "You can disagree with me."], [728.5, "That's fine."], [729.4, "If you disagree with me, go to the forums and tell me that AJ, you're totally wrong."], [734.1, "That's fine."], [735.0, "If you agree with me, that's also great."], [737.1, "Write that."], [738.0, "Okay, I'll see you next time, bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["emotionally intelligent", "/ɪˈməʊʃənəli ɪnˈtelɪdʒənt/", "thông minh cảm xúc"], ["newlywed", "/ˈnjuːliwed/", "mới cưới"], ["indicate", "/ˈɪndɪkeɪt/", "cho thấy"], ["transform", "/trænsˈfɔːm/", "thay đổi, biến đổi"], ["fall into the category of", "/fɔːl ˈɪntə ðə ˈkætəɡəri ɒv/", "thuộc nhóm"], ["decade", "/ˈdekeɪd/", "thập kỷ"], ["used to be", "/juːst tə biː/", "đã từng là"], ["honor", "/ˈɒnə/", "trân trọng, tôn vinh"], ["be open to", "/bi ˈəʊpən tuː/", "sẵn lòng đón nhận"], ["emote", "/ɪˈməʊt/", "bộc lộ cảm xúc"], ["connect", "/kəˈnekt/", "kết nối"], ["choose A over B", "/tʃuːz ˈeɪ ˈəʊvə biː/", "chọn A thay vì B"], ["evolution", "/ˌiːvəˈluːʃn/", "sự tiến hóa"], ["superior to", "/suːˈpɪəriə tuː/", "hơn, vượt trội hơn"], ["upbringing", "/ˈʌpbrɪŋɪŋ/", "sự giáo dục, nuôi dạy"], ["moral fiber", "/ˈmɒrəl ˈfaɪbə/", "phẩm chất đạo đức"], ["figure out", "/ˈfɪɡər aʊt/", "nhận ra, tìm ra"], ["convey", "/kənˈveɪ/", "truyền đạt, thể hiện"], ["elementary", "/ˌelɪˈmentri/", "cơ bản, đơn giản"], ["priority", "/praɪˈɒrəti/", "ưu tiên"], ["revise", "/rɪˈvaɪz/", "sửa đổi"], ["admiration", "/ˌædməˈreɪʃn/", "sự ngưỡng mộ"], ["fondness", "/ˈfɒndnəs/", "sự yêu mến"], ["turn toward", "/tɜːn təˈwɔːd/", "hướng về"], ["benefit", "/ˈbenɪfɪt/", "có lợi cho"], ["accept influence", "/əkˈsept ˈɪnfluəns/", "chấp nhận ảnh hưởng"], ["outstanding", "/aʊtˈstændɪŋ/", "xuất sắc"], ["troubled", "/ˈtrʌbld/", "lo âu, gặp chuyện"], ["delighted", "/dɪˈlaɪtɪd/", "vui mừng"], ["mourn", "/mɔːn/", "thương tiếc"], ["entitlement", "/ɪnˈtaɪtlmənt/", "đặc quyền"], ["righteous indignation", "/ˈraɪtʃəs ˌɪndɪɡˈneɪʃn/", "sự phẫn nộ chính đáng"], ["victim", "/ˈvɪktɪm/", "nạn nhân"], ["authoritarian", "/ɔːˌθɒrɪˈteəriən/", "độc đoán"], ["withdraw into a shell", "/wɪðˈdrɔː ˈɪntə ə ʃel/", "thu mình vào vỏ ốc"], ["one's due", "/wʌnz djuː/", "điều mình xứng đáng nhận"], ["consequence", "/ˈkɒnsɪkwəns/", "hậu quả"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["more husbands are being transformed", "ngày càng nhiều người chồng đang thay đổi"], ["fall into the category of", "thuộc nhóm"], ["the number used to be much lower", "con số từng thấp hơn nhiều"], ["open to learning more about emotions", "sẵn lòng học thêm về cảm xúc"], ["connect with her emotionally", "kết nối với cô ấy về cảm xúc"], ["he'll turn off the TV and listen", "anh ấy sẽ tắt TV và lắng nghe"], ["choosing \"us\" over \"me\"", "chọn \"chúng ta\" thay vì \"tôi\""], ["the next step in social evolution", "bước tiếp theo của sự tiến hóa xã hội"], ["superior to other men", "hơn những người đàn ông khác"], ["It is really that elementary.", "Thực sự chỉ đơn giản vậy thôi."], ["make his career less of a priority", "đặt sự nghiệp xuống hàng thứ yếu"], ["his definition of success has been revised", "định nghĩa thành công của anh ấy đã thay đổi"], ["keeps in touch with his admiration and fondness", "luôn giữ sự ngưỡng mộ và yêu mến"], ["not only his marriage, but his children as well", "không chỉ hôn nhân mà cả con cái"], ["accept influence from his wife", "chấp nhận ảnh hưởng từ vợ"], ["leads a meaningful and rich life", "sống một cuộc đời ý nghĩa và phong phú"], ["not only when she is troubled, but when she is delighted", "không chỉ khi buồn mà cả khi vui"], ["the people who matter most to him", "những người quan trọng nhất với anh"], ["withdraw into a lonely shell", "thu mình vào vỏ ốc cô đơn"], ["what little he has left", "chút ít những gì còn lại"], ["the respect he thinks is his due", "sự tôn trọng anh ta nghĩ mình xứng đáng nhận"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["My data / Research + indicate(s) / show(s) that + clause", "Research shows that sleep improves memory.", "Nghiên cứu cho thấy giấc ngủ giúp cải thiện trí nhớ.", "shows that|indicate that|indicates that"], ["S + fall(s) into the category of + noun", "These books fall into the category of fiction.", "Những cuốn sách này thuộc thể loại hư cấu.", "category"], ["S + used to be + adj", "This street used to be quiet.", "Con phố này từng rất yên tĩnh.", "used to be"], ["S + be + open to + V-ing", "I'm open to trying new food.", "Tôi sẵn lòng thử món mới.", "open to"], ["S + come(s) to + V (understand/realize/love)", "Over time, I came to love this city.", "Theo thời gian, tôi dần yêu thành phố này.", "come to|came to"], ["S + choose(s) + A + over + B", "She chose her family over her career.", "Cô ấy chọn gia đình thay vì sự nghiệp.", "over"], ["This doesn't mean that + clause", "This doesn't mean that you are wrong.", "Điều này không có nghĩa là bạn sai.", "doesn't mean"], ["S + be + superior to + noun", "This phone is superior to the old one.", "Chiếc điện thoại này tốt hơn chiếc cũ.", "superior to"], ["S + be + likely to + V", "It's likely to rain tomorrow.", "Ngày mai có khả năng mưa.", "likely to"], ["Unlike + noun, S + V", "Unlike his brother, he loves sports.", "Không giống anh trai, cậu ấy rất thích thể thao.", "unlike"], ["S + benefit(s) not only A, but B as well", "Exercise benefits not only your body, but your mind as well.", "Tập thể dục không chỉ có lợi cho cơ thể mà cả tinh thần.", "not only"], ["S + tend(s) to be + noun/adj", "Small children tend to be curious.", "Trẻ nhỏ thường hay tò mò.", "tends to|tend to"], ["V-ing + makes it possible for + someone + to V", "Having a car makes it possible for me to travel more.", "Có xe giúp tôi đi lại nhiều hơn.", "makes it possible"], ["Because + S + will not + V, S + will not + V", "Because he won't listen, he won't learn.", "Vì không chịu nghe nên anh ta sẽ không học được.", "because"]]$j$::jsonb
)
