-- ── Bài 18: Lifestyle Diseases (chữ từ audio bằng Whisper, đã soát) ──
insert into public.effortless_lessons (course, lesson_no, slug, title, level, description, cover, main_audio, vocab_audio, ms_audio, pov_audio, com_audio, main_story, mini_story, ms_parts, pov_story, com_story, vocab, phrases, patterns)
values (
  'Original Course',
  18,
  'lifestyle-diseases',
  'Lifestyle Diseases',
  'intermediate',
  'Bài viết về các bệnh do lối sống: béo phì, tiểu đường, và vì sao thay đổi suy nghĩ mới là chìa khóa để giảm cân. Học cách nói về sức khỏe, ăn uống và thói quen.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1512621776951-a57141f2eefd',
  'Original_Course/118a Lifestyle Diseases (main).mp3',
  'Original_Course/118b Lifestyle Diseases (vocabulary).mp3',
  'Original_Course/118c Lifestyle Diseases (ms).mp3',
  null,
  null,
  $j$[[0.1, "Lifestyle Diseases, by Shiori Iwagaki", "Các bệnh do lối sống, của Shiori Iwagaki"], [5.1, "The major contributing factor to lifestyle-related diseases, typified by diabetes, high blood pressure and heart disease, is often obesity.", "Yếu tố góp phần chính gây ra các bệnh liên quan đến lối sống, tiêu biểu là tiểu đường, cao huyết áp và bệnh tim, thường là béo phì."], [16.3, "Therefore, we have to think about losing surplus weight.", "Vì vậy, chúng ta phải nghĩ đến việc giảm số cân thừa."], [20.6, "When I was watching TV the other day, I found a program which tried to introduce a way to cook low-calorie dishes.", "Hôm trước khi xem TV, tôi thấy một chương trình giới thiệu cách nấu các món ít calo."], [26.5, "It showed food images for a full hour.", "Chương trình chiếu hình ảnh đồ ăn suốt một tiếng đồng hồ."], [30.1, "Then they let three overweight guests eat three full servings of curry rice, Japanese-style curry with rice.", "Sau đó họ cho ba vị khách thừa cân ăn ba suất cơm cà ri đầy đủ, kiểu cà ri Nhật ăn với cơm."], [38.2, "The dishes were made with lower calories than normal, but that tasting totaled 1,800 calories.", "Các món được nấu ít calo hơn bình thường, nhưng bữa nếm thử đó tổng cộng lên tới 1.800 calo."], [45.6, "If you have a chance to visit America, in which many people are struggling to lose excess weight, try watching TV.", "Nếu có dịp đến Mỹ, nơi nhiều người đang vật lộn để giảm cân thừa, hãy thử xem TV."], [53.4, "You will find it is filled with food commercials and medicines that are supposed to help you lose fat.", "Bạn sẽ thấy TV đầy quảng cáo đồ ăn và thuốc được cho là giúp bạn giảm mỡ."], [60.2, "However, the best way to lose weight is not by eating low-calorie food, but by reducing the amount of food you eat.", "Tuy nhiên, cách giảm cân tốt nhất không phải là ăn đồ ít calo, mà là giảm lượng thức ăn bạn ăn."], [69.5, "And it's really difficult to reduce your meal portion sizes while surrounded by actual food or images of food on TV, unless you have an unbelievably strong will.", "Và thật sự rất khó giảm khẩu phần ăn khi xung quanh toàn là đồ ăn thật hoặc hình ảnh đồ ăn trên TV, trừ khi bạn có ý chí mạnh khó tin."], [81.1, "So, it is very important to keep away from this toxic food environment.", "Vì vậy, điều rất quan trọng là tránh xa môi trường đồ ăn độc hại này."], [86.6, "But avoiding food advertising images is still not enough, because if you want to lose weight, changing your physical environment is not enough.", "Nhưng tránh hình ảnh quảng cáo đồ ăn vẫn chưa đủ, vì nếu muốn giảm cân, chỉ thay đổi môi trường vật chất là chưa đủ."], [96.0, "What is most important is to keep your mental environment free of unhealthy food images.", "Điều quan trọng nhất là giữ cho môi trường tinh thần không có những hình ảnh đồ ăn không lành mạnh."], [102.3, "This is important for all of us.", "Điều này quan trọng với tất cả chúng ta."], [104.9, "We have to find a way to shift our mental focus from food to healthier foci, such as sports, reading or music.", "Chúng ta phải tìm cách chuyển sự tập trung trong đầu từ đồ ăn sang những thứ lành mạnh hơn, như thể thao, đọc sách hay âm nhạc."], [114.6, "Perhaps instead of calling them lifestyle-related diseases, we should call them thought-related diseases, for thought and emotion are the true root causes of these diseases.", "Có lẽ thay vì gọi là bệnh liên quan đến lối sống, ta nên gọi là bệnh liên quan đến suy nghĩ, vì suy nghĩ và cảm xúc mới là căn nguyên thực sự của những bệnh này."], [126.9, "If we are always worried and anxious, we may eat as an outlet for these feelings.", "Nếu lúc nào cũng lo lắng và bồn chồn, ta có thể ăn để giải tỏa những cảm xúc đó."], [132.2, "If we constantly think of failure and problems, we may eat as a way to distract ourselves from these thoughts.", "Nếu liên tục nghĩ về thất bại và rắc rối, ta có thể ăn như một cách để quên đi những suy nghĩ đó."], [140.1, "Therefore, it is our negative thoughts and emotions, and our inappropriate way of dealing with them, that is the true cause of obesity and lifestyle-related diseases.", "Vì vậy, chính những suy nghĩ, cảm xúc tiêu cực và cách xử lý chúng không phù hợp mới là nguyên nhân thực sự của béo phì và các bệnh do lối sống."], [150.7, "So, our challenge is to shift our thoughts and emotions, and to handle the negative ones in a better way.", "Vì thế, thử thách của chúng ta là thay đổi suy nghĩ và cảm xúc, và xử lý những điều tiêu cực theo cách tốt hơn."], [158.0, "This is the best way to lose weight and gain health.", "Đây là cách tốt nhất để giảm cân và có sức khỏe."], [161.7, "We can enjoy the satisfaction of finishing a really fat book.", "Chúng ta có thể tận hưởng niềm vui khi đọc xong một cuốn sách thật dày."], [166.0, "We can enjoy the achievement of passing a difficult exam.", "Chúng ta có thể tận hưởng thành tựu khi vượt qua một kỳ thi khó."], [169.9, "We can enjoy the exertion and effort of sports.", "Chúng ta có thể tận hưởng sự gắng sức và nỗ lực khi chơi thể thao."], [173.5, "Of course, we can enumerate many more positive pursuits.", "Tất nhiên, chúng ta có thể kể ra thêm nhiều hoạt động tích cực khác."], [177.7, "The point is, changing our mental focus is the key.", "Vấn đề là, thay đổi sự tập trung trong đầu mới là chìa khóa."], [182.0, "There are many ways to cultivate a healthy mental environment.", "Có nhiều cách để nuôi dưỡng một môi trường tinh thần lành mạnh."], [185.7, "We don't even have to wait.", "Chúng ta thậm chí không cần chờ đợi."], [187.8, "Today or tomorrow, we can start to think in a different way.", "Ngay hôm nay hoặc ngày mai, chúng ta có thể bắt đầu suy nghĩ theo cách khác."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.2, "s", "Okay, welcome to the mini-story for the Lifestyle Diseases article."], [6.8, "s", "These stories are not serious, I'm sure you realize."], [11.3, "s", "They're not supposed to be serious."], [12.9, "s", "They're just funny, foolish, stupid little stories to help you remember some of the new vocabulary and also to help you know how to use this vocabulary in other situations."], [26.9, "s", "So just listen, just relax, don't take this seriously."], [31.1, "s", "But the more you listen, the more you will understand the vocabulary and how to use it."], [36.1, "s", "Let's get started."], [37.2, "s", "Here's our story for today."], [40.1, "s", "There once was a guy named AJ."], [43.6, "s", "AJ had a lot of excess energy."], [47.0, "s", "He was constantly anxious."], [49.6, "s", "This distracted him."], [51.6, "s", "He could never handle all the surplus energy he had."], [54.8, "s", "He couldn't focus on just one thing."], [58.5, "s", "His mind constantly jumped between many foci."], [63.4, "s", "AJ needed an outlet for all this energy."], [66.7, "s", "He thought that physical exertion might help, so he practiced many sports."], [72.6, "s", "To enumerate just a few, he practiced basketball, baseball, football, American football, soccer, volleyball, swimming, etc."], [84.2, "s", "But these pursuits didn't solve the problem."], [88.3, "s", "AJ still had too much energy."], [91.2, "s", "So AJ finally decided to discover the root cause of his problem."], [96.7, "s", "He realized he was too nervous and crazy, and he needed to calm down."], [102.5, "s", "So he decided to cultivate a peaceful mind."], [108.2, "s", "He meditated every day."], [111.8, "s", "Gradually, his mind calmed and became less distracted."], [117.4, "s", "In the end, AJ decided to cut all his hair off."], [122.2, "s", "He moved to a mountain and lived in a cave for the rest of his life."], [127.5, "s", "The end."], [129.4, "s", "Okay, one more time."], [131.0, "s", "This time, I'll ask a lot of questions."], [133.8, "s", "The reason I ask questions is to help you remember some of the vocabulary and to know how to use it."], [142.5, "s", "Alright, well let's go."], [144.4, "s", "There once was a guy named AJ."], [148.2, "s", "AJ had a lot of excess energy."], [152.0, "q", "Now did AJ have too much energy?"], [154.9, "a", "Yes he did of course, he had excess energy."], [158.1, "q", "Did he have just enough energy?"], [160.5, "a", "No, he had excess energy."], [162.4, "s", "It was too much."], [164.2, "s", "He was constantly anxious."], [167.1, "q", "Was he relaxed?"], [168.8, "a", "No."], [169.9, "q", "Did he feel good?"], [171.2, "a", "No, he did not."], [171.9, "s", "He felt anxious."], [172.9, "s", "He felt very nervous."], [174.4, "s", "He was always nervous, so he was very, very anxious."], [178.8, "q", "Did this help him to focus his mind?"], [182.6, "a", "No, it did not."], [183.5, "s", "It had the opposite it affect, this anxiety, this anxiousness distracted him."], [189.9, "s", "Because he had too much energy, because he was anxious, he was very distracted."], [194.7, "s", "He would always change his mind."], [196.9, "s", "He could never focus on one thing."], [199.8, "s", "His energy distracted him."], [204.0, "s", "He could never handle all the surplus energy he had."], [209.0, "q", "Did he have a good solution for this energy?"], [213.2, "a", "No, he couldn't handle it."], [214.9, "s", "He couldn't handle it."], [216.0, "s", "Did he deal with this energy in a good way?"], [218.7, "q", "Could he survive and use this energy in a good way?"], [222.6, "a", "No, he could not."], [223.3, "s", "He could not handle the energy."], [225.5, "s", "It was too much."], [226.4, "s", "He couldn't handle it."], [227.6, "s", "He couldn't solve this problem."], [230.4, "q", "Did he have too much energy?"], [232.2, "a", "Of course, that's the problem."], [233.7, "s", "He had surplus energy."], [236.2, "q", "Now, did AJ have surplus money?"], [239.0, "a", "No, he did not have surplus money."], [241.6, "q", "What was his problem?"], [242.9, "a", "Well, his problem was that he had surplus energy."], [245.9, "s", "Too much energy."], [247.4, "s", "He couldn't focus on just one thing."], [250.7, "s", "So, his mind did not focus on one thing, such as reading or a movie."], [255.4, "s", "Instead, it jumped between many different foci."], [258.8, "s", "So, one second, he's looking at a book, the next second he's looking at a movie, the next second he's thinking about food, the next second he's watching a pretty girl."], [268.1, "s", "So his mind has these all these foci jumps between them all the time."], [272.7, "s", "Too many foci in the world and AJ could not focus on only one of them."], [277.9, "s", "Instead his mind would jump from foci to foci to foci."], [281.6, "s", "Alright, all these different foci."], [284.9, "s", "AJ needed an outlet for this energy, right?"], [287.7, "s", "He needed to get rid of this energy somehow."], [290.9, "s", "He had to use it or burn it or get rid of it, because he couldn't handle all of it."], [298.0, "s", "So he decided, I need an outlet for this energy, right?"], [301.9, "s", "I need to use the energy somehow and get rid of it."], [306.1, "s", "I need an outlet."], [307.6, "s", "So what was his outlet?"], [309.3, "s", "What kind of outlet did AJ try?"], [311.8, "q", "Did AJ try to use reading as an outlet?"], [315.0, "a", "No, AJ decided that physical exertion would be the best outlet."], [318.9, "s", "He decided physical exercise, using his body, picking a big effort with his body, right?"], [325.7, "s", "Physical exertion would be the best outlet for all this energy."], [329.6, "s", "So AJ tried a lot of physical exertion."], [332.4, "s", "He practiced a lot of sports."], [335.2, "s", "Now, we're going to list these sports, right?"], [337.3, "s", "We're going to make a list of a few of these sports."], [343.0, "s", "We're going to enumerate these sports, we're going to list them."], [348