  $j$[[0.6, "Okay, welcome to the commentary for the Microsoft Censorship article."], [8.7, "Of course, Microsoft, in fact, is not the only company that is censoring, especially in China."], [16.2, "Yahoo has also been helping the Chinese government."], [19.3, "And I believe Google is also censoring their search results in China."], [26.4, "So, it's a big problem."], [28.5, "One of the reasons I included this article."], [31.3, "And I want to start including more articles on more topics."], [37.4, "And I want to focus on topics that are not just average topics."], [42.1, "I guess with effortless English, I've thought a lot about the purpose of effortless English."], [47.3, "Of course."], [48.5, "Purpose number one is to help people learn English in an enjoyable way, enjoy learning English, Spanish, reading articles that are not from textbooks and listening to articles and listening to lessons that are not based on textbooks, because I think textbooks are just horrible."], [66.8, "And as a student, I think they're horrible, learning Spanish."], [70.1, "And as a teacher, I think they're terrible, too."], [72.0, "So I don't like textbooks."], [73.7, "I also don't like grammar study, grammar analysis."], [77.8, "I think you should use a grammar book the same way you use a dictionary."], [82.2, "And so if you have a question about grammar, you find some grammar in an article, you don't understand it."], [88.0, "So yeah, you look in the grammar book, you find what it means, you find what it is."], [92.7, "Then you understand it."], [93.8, "Okay, put the grammar book away."], [96.1, "Unfortunately, most schools and a lot of students use the grammar book like some kind of Bible."], [102.9, "And they almost try to memorize it and they focus so much on the grammar book."], [106.7, "And that actually hurts your speaking ability."], [111.4, "It hurts your English ability."], [113.4, "It is not a good thing to do."], [115.7, "So use the grammar book just like you use the dictionary as a reference."], [120.4, "Something to refer to, to look at, and then you put it away."], [124.4, "That's all you need to do with the grammar book."], [126.4, "I'm not saying grammar is totally bad, I'm just saying use it correctly."], [130.5, "Use the grammar book correctly."], [131.5, "So anyway."], [133.3, "The point is that effortless English, I wanted to do it as a club."], [139.2, "As a community."], [140.8, "And that had some deeper meaning, not only just learning English."], [145.6, "Of course that's our main goal."], [147.9, "But I also wanted to do something kind of like what some companies like The Body Shop tried to do."], [157.0, "Ben and Jerry's for a while tried to do this."], [159.6, "There are some companies that also had other goals."], [163.6, "Not just their primary goal, their main goal of selling something or making something, but also they had deeper values, deeper principles."], [174.0, "And I guess I'm kind of a liberal, progressive person, and I wanted to include that in effortless English also."], [181.9, "And so this article is my first attempt to do that, and that is to include human rights information."], [189.3, "Human rights articles."], [190.8, "And I'm going to try to do this more often."], [193.3, "Human rights are important to me."], [195.3, "By human rights, I mean, you know."], [197.5, "The rights of all human beings to have free speech."], [203.0, "To not be killed by their governments just because they disagree with the government."], [210.6, "Anyway, basically."], [212.5, "The rights that you find in the American, the Constitution."], [216.3, "The U.S., United States Constitution."], [218.7, "which we call the Bill of Rights."], [221.2, "The Bill of Rights guarantees freedom of speech."], [224.1, "Freedom of assembly."], [225.1, "That means you can get together with other people without worrying about the government"], [230.6, "arresting you, or you can protest against the government if you want to."], [234.8, "There's a long list of them."], [235.9, "And the UN also has a similar list of human rights."], [240.7, "And of course, most governments have this kind of list."], [244.2, "They have these human rights."], [245.9, "Almost every government in the world says, yes, yes, we respect human rights."], [250.1, "And, you know, the Chinese government certainly does, the American government does."], [253.8, "They all do it."], [255.0, "But the problem is, of course, they don't really follow these rights."], [260.5, "They don't really respect them."], [262.3, "And I'm not picking on, I'm not bullying China."], [264.7, "America has problems, too."], [266.9, "I think I'd like to include an article about Guantanamo soon."], [271.5, "About this prison America has in Cuba."], [274.3, "Where we're putting all these people without lawyers, without any kind of human rights at all, and we're putting them there forever, possibly forever."], [284.8, "I mean, these people have no chance to go to a regular court to have lawyers."], [289.2, "Many of them are innocent, many of them who have been released."], [292.8, "It's found out they were innocent, they did nothing wrong."], [295.9, "So anyway, this is an important issue for me in the world."], [298.8, "In America it's important, in all the world."], [301.2, "So I want to start including more information, more articles about human rights."], [305.1, "It's something that I would like effortless English to stand for a little bit."], [310.7, "A value that we would have here."], [313.0, "Another value I think would be."], [315.1, "That it's important to me would be the environment."], [318.2, "Especially issues like global warming."], [322.2, "Again, it's an issue that affects all of us, everywhere in the world."], [327.2, "And I would like to start including some articles, some information about that, some lessons about that."], [333.1, "I would especially love to see some discussions, some forum discussions about these topics."], [339.9, "Where we could introduce more information to each other and discuss these topics."], [343.9, "Because I think it's important if we're learning English."], [347.0, "Why are most people learning English on this site?"], [350.4, "I think it's because English is an international language."], [353.1, "Right now, at least, it's probably the main international language."], [358.6, "English is the easiest way to communicate with people from many different countries."], [364.4, "If you want to talk to someone in Japan, and you want to talk to an African person, and a European person, and someone in another Asian country, and someone in Latin America..."], [376.9, "Well English is the language that we all have decided we will use if we get together in an international group."], [384.7, "In science, in education, in government."], [389.1, "So for that reason, right now, it's an international language."], [393.4, "English does not belong to America."], [396.2, "English does not belong to England."], [399.3, "In fact, English belongs to the whole world now."], [401.9, "And so I think we should focus a little bit on these global issues."], [408.6, "These issues that affect all of us."], [410.7, "The idea of respecting human life everywhere, in every country."], [415.4, "Human rights all over the world."], [418.0, "And the idea of protecting the planet, the environment."], [422.2, "About learning more about global warming and what we can do about it."], [427.4, "These are international issues."], [429.1, "And I think that because English is an international language right now."], [434.8, "And because this club certainly is international, we have people from every continent."], [440.3, "Except Antarctica, I think."], [443.4, "So I want to start focusing on some of those things and start focusing on some values, some principles."], [449.9, "Other than just language learning."], [453.7, "Language learning is great, but why are we learning language?"], [457.0, "We're learning it to communicate."], [458.4, "We're learning it to build an international community."], [462.3, "That's what I think about when I work on effortless English."], [466.9, "I want to make our club into a community, an international community where we respect each other."], [473.3, "where we learn from each other,"], [476.7, "and where we promote things like human rights for all people everywhere."], [482.5, "So anyway, that's the reason I included this first article about Microsoft censoring in China."], [490.5, "China is just one example."], [492.4, "These kind of things are happening in lots of countries."], [495.3, "Burma has a large problem."], [497.1, "Here in America, we have many problems."], [498.7, "And I'm happy to write about those as well."], [503.0, "In fact, I'm very happy to write about those."], [505.5, "Another reason I thought about this article was interesting is because the issue of cyber censorship, censorship on the internet."], [512.2, "Because, again, we are an Internet club, right?"], [516.3, "We're an Internet-based club."], [517.6, "We're learning English on the Internet."], [519.6, "We're communicating with each other on the Internet."], [522.0, "And so I think this issue is very important to us because if companies like Microsoft start censoring content on the Internet, we all suffer."], [531.4, "It affects all of us."], [533.3, "This first guy that they censored, this Chinese guy, he was writing in Beijing, but his blog was hosted on servers, on computers, in the United States."], [544.7, "And they were removed."], [546.2, "So not only was this guy, what's his name?"], [549.7, "Michael Enti or Zhao Jing."], [552.4, "He was censored not only in China, he was censored all over the world."], [557.7, "Readers everywhere could not read his blog."], [561.6, "And so that's a very serious issue, I think."], [564.1, "So it's important for us to be informed about these things and put some pressure so that we can continue to talk about any issue we want here at Effortless English."], [576.4, "In your email, in your personal blogs."], [579.2, "On your own websites."], [581.1, "From the news you get on the internet."], [583.8, "It's important, I think, that we keep that information open and that we're aware when companies like Microsoft try to limit that information."], [592.7, "So that's a big, it's an important issue, I think, as well."], [598.1, "So those are a couple of reasons why I think this global censorship idea, internet censorship, it's a very important idea that we should focus on."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["censorship", "/ˈsensəʃɪp/", "sự kiểm duyệt"], ["censor", "/ˈsensə/", "kiểm duyệt"], ["cooperate with", "/kəʊˈɒpəreɪt wɪð/", "hợp tác với"], ["authorities", "/ɔːˈθɒrətiz/", "nhà chức trách"], ["shut down", "/ʃʌt daʊn/", "đóng cửa, ngừng hoạt động"], ["controversial", "/ˌkɒntrəˈvɜːʃl/", "gây tranh cãi"], ["critic", "/ˈkrɪtɪk/", "người chỉ trích"], ["host", "/həʊst/", "lưu trữ (trang web)"], ["server", "/ˈsɜːvə/", "máy chủ"], ["globally", "/ˈɡləʊbəli/", "trên toàn cầu"], ["criticism", "/ˈkrɪtɪsɪzəm/", "lời chỉ trích"], ["claim", "/kleɪm/", "tuyên bố"], ["implement", "/ˈɪmplɪment/", "thực hiện, áp dụng"], ["ensure", "/ɪnˈʃɔː/", "đảm bảo"], ["formal legal notice", "/ˈfɔːml ˈliːɡl ˈnəʊtɪs/", "thông báo pháp lý chính thức"], ["deny access", "/dɪˈnaɪ ˈækses/", "từ chối quyền truy cập"], ["search engine", "/sɜːtʃ ˈendʒɪn/", "công cụ tìm kiếm"], ["filter", "/ˈfɪltə/", "lọc"], ["sensitive", "/ˈsensətɪv/", "nhạy cảm"], ["undertake", "/ˌʌndəˈteɪk/", "thực hiện"], ["massacre", "/ˈmæsəkə/", "vụ thảm sát"], ["furthermore", "/ˌfɜːðəˈmɔː/", "hơn nữa"], ["admit", "/ədˈmɪt/", "thừa nhận"], ["restrict", "/rɪˈstrɪkt/", "hạn chế"], ["caption", "/ˈkæpʃn/", "chú thích"], ["assert", "/əˈsɜːt/", "khẳng định"], ["at odds with", "/ət ɒdz wɪð/", "mâu thuẫn với"], ["launch", "/lɔːntʃ/", "ra mắt"], ["human rights", "/ˈhjuːmən raɪts/", "nhân quyền"], ["freedom of expression", "/ˈfriːdəm ɒv ɪkˈspreʃn/", "tự do ngôn luận"], ["prohibited", "/prəˈhɪbɪtɪd/", "bị cấm"], ["profanity", "/prəˈfænəti/", "lời tục tĩu"], ["demonstrate", "/ˈdemənstreɪt/", "chứng minh, cho thấy"], ["the full range of", "/ðə fʊl reɪndʒ ɒv/", "toàn bộ"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["cooperated with Chinese authorities", "hợp tác với chính quyền Trung Quốc"], ["shut down the controversial blog", "đóng blog gây tranh cãi"], ["an active critic of censorship", "người tích cực chỉ trích kiểm duyệt"], ["hosted on servers located in the United States", "lưu trữ trên máy chủ đặt tại Mỹ"], ["not only in China, but globally", "không chỉ ở Trung Quốc mà trên toàn cầu"], ["Reacting to criticism", "Trước những lời chỉ trích"], ["claims to have implemented a new set of standards", "tuyên bố đã áp dụng bộ tiêu chuẩn mới"], ["access will only be denied to users in China", "chỉ chặn truy cập với người dùng ở Trung Quốc"], ["politically sensitive terms", "những từ nhạy cảm về chính trị"], ["certain content was removed", "một số nội dung đã bị xóa"], ["responds to directions from the government", "làm theo chỉ thị của chính phủ"], ["do not filter blog content in any way", "không lọc nội dung blog theo bất kỳ cách nào"], ["at odds with the facts", "trái ngược với sự thật"], ["freedom of expression", "tự do ngôn luận"], ["Please type a different title.", "Vui lòng nhập tiêu đề khác."], ["As a result of such actions", "Do những hành động như vậy"], ["the full range of information", "toàn bộ thông tin"], ["To learn more, go to", "Để tìm hiểu thêm, hãy vào"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["S + cooperate(d) with + someone + to + V", "We cooperated with the school to plant trees.", "Chúng tôi hợp tác với trường để trồng cây.", "cooperated with|cooperate with"], ["..., which was + V3 + ..., was + V3", "The house, which was built in 1900, was sold.", "Ngôi nhà, được xây năm 1900, đã được bán.", "which was"], ["not only A, but (also) B", "She is not only smart, but also kind.", "Cô ấy không chỉ thông minh mà còn tốt bụng.", "not only"], ["V-ing to + noun, S + V", "Reacting to the news, he called his mother.", "Trước tin đó, anh ấy gọi cho mẹ.", "reacting to"], ["S + claim(s) to have + V3", "He claims to have met the president.", "Anh ta tuyên bố đã gặp tổng thống.", "claims to have|claim to have"], ["S + V + to ensure that + clause", "Check twice to ensure that nothing is missing.", "Kiểm tra hai lần để đảm bảo không thiếu gì.", "ensure that"], ["S + only + V + when + clause", "I only drink coffee when I'm tired.", "Tôi chỉ uống cà phê khi mệt.", "only"], ["Furthermore, + clause", "The hotel is cheap. Furthermore, it's near the beach.", "Khách sạn rẻ. Hơn nữa, nó gần biển.", "furthermore"], ["S + has admitted that + clause", "He has admitted that he was wrong.", "Anh ấy đã thừa nhận mình sai.", "admitted"], ["S + restrict(s) + someone + from + V-ing", "The rules restrict students from using phones.", "Quy định hạn chế học sinh dùng điện thoại.", "restricting|restrict|from using"], ["S + consider(s) + noun + to be + adj", "Many people consider him to be a genius.", "Nhiều người coi anh ấy là thiên tài.", "considers|consider|to be"], ["S + be + at odds with + noun", "His words are at odds with his actions.", "Lời nói của anh ta mâu thuẫn với hành động.", "at odds"], ["As a result of + noun, S + V", "As a result of the storm, the school closed.", "Do bão, trường học đóng cửa.", "as a result"], ["S + be + denied + the ability to + V", "Prisoners are denied the ability to vote.", "Tù nhân bị tước quyền bầu cử.", "denied"]]$j$::jsonb
)
