-- ── Bài 24: No Belief (chữ từ audio bằng Whisper, đã soát) ──
insert into public.effortless_lessons (course, lesson_no, slug, title, level, description, cover, main_audio, vocab_audio, ms_audio, pov_audio, com_audio, main_story, mini_story, ms_parts, pov_story, com_story, vocab, phrases, patterns)
values (
  'Original Course',
  24,
  'no-belief',
  'No Belief',
  'intermediate',
  'Bài luận "I don''t believe anything": niềm tin cứng nhắc là cái chết của trí tuệ, "bản đồ không phải là lãnh thổ". Học cách nói về niềm tin, khoa học và tư duy cởi mở — kèm lời bình của A.J.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1628498188904-036f5e25e93e',
  'Original_Course/124a No Belief (main).mp3',
  'Original_Course/124b No Belief (vocabulary).mp3',
  'Original_Course/124c No Belief (ms).mp3',
  null,
  'Original_Course/124e No Belief (com).mp3',
  $j$[[2.3, "No Belief", "Không niềm tin"], [5.1, "This remark was made, in these very words, by John Gribbin, physics editor of New Scientist magazine, in a BBC TV debate with Malcolm Muggeridge, and it provoked incredulity on the part of most viewers.", "Câu nói này, đúng từng chữ như vậy, là của John Gribbin, biên tập viên mảng vật lý của tạp chí New Scientist, trong một cuộc tranh luận trên kênh BBC với Malcolm Muggeridge, và nó khiến phần lớn khán giả không tin nổi."], [18.9, "It seems to be a hangover of the medieval Catholic Church that causes most people, even the educated, to think that everybody must believe something or other.", "Dường như chính tàn dư của Giáo hội Công giáo thời trung cổ khiến phần lớn mọi người, kể cả người có học, nghĩ rằng ai cũng phải tin vào một điều gì đó."], [29.8, "That if one is not a theist, one must be a dogmatic atheist; and if one does not think capitalism is perfect, one must believe fervently in socialism; and if one does not have blind faith in X, one must alternatively have blind faith in not-X, or the reverse of X.", "Rằng nếu không tin có Chúa thì ắt phải là người vô thần giáo điều; nếu không cho rằng chủ nghĩa tư bản hoàn hảo thì ắt phải tin cuồng nhiệt vào chủ nghĩa xã hội; và nếu không mù quáng tin vào X thì ắt phải mù quáng tin vào không-X, tức điều ngược lại với X."], [50.9, "My own opinion is that belief is the death of intelligence.", "Theo tôi, niềm tin là cái chết của trí tuệ."], [55.3, "As soon as one believes a doctrine of any sort or assumes certitude, one stops thinking about that aspect of existence.", "Ngay khi người ta tin vào một học thuyết nào đó hay cho rằng mình chắc chắn, người ta ngừng suy nghĩ về khía cạnh đó của sự tồn tại."], [63.6, "The more certitude one assumes, the less there is left to think about, and a person sure of everything would never have any need to think about anything, and might be considered clinically dead under current medical standards, where absence of brain activity is taken to mean that life has ended.", "Người ta càng cho rằng mình chắc chắn thì càng ít điều còn lại để suy nghĩ, và một người chắc chắn về mọi thứ sẽ chẳng bao giờ cần nghĩ về điều gì, và có thể bị coi là đã chết lâm sàng theo tiêu chuẩn y học hiện nay, khi việc não ngừng hoạt động được hiểu là sự sống đã chấm dứt."], [83.0, "My attitude is identical to that of Dr. Gribbin and the majority of physicists today, and it is known in physics as the Copenhagen Interpretation, because it was formulated in Copenhagen by Dr. Niels Bohr and his co-workers between 1926 and 1928.", "Thái độ của tôi giống hệt với tiến sĩ Gribbin và phần lớn các nhà vật lý ngày nay, và trong vật lý nó được gọi là Cách diễn giải Copenhagen, vì nó được tiến sĩ Niels Bohr và các cộng sự đưa ra ở Copenhagen trong khoảng 1926 đến 1928."], [100.7, "The Copenhagen Interpretation is sometimes called model agnosticism, and says that any grid we use to organize our experience of the world is a model of the world, and should not be confused with the world itself.", "Cách diễn giải Copenhagen đôi khi được gọi là thuyết bất khả tri về mô hình, cho rằng bất kỳ khung nào ta dùng để sắp xếp trải nghiệm về thế giới cũng chỉ là một mô hình của thế giới, và không nên nhầm lẫn với chính thế giới."], [115.5, "Alfred Korzybski tried to popularize this outside physics with the slogan, \"The map is not the territory.\"", "Alfred Korzybski đã cố phổ biến ý này ra ngoài giới vật lý bằng khẩu hiệu: \"Bản đồ không phải là lãnh thổ.\""], [123.5, "Alan Watts, a talented Oriental philosopher, restated it more vividly as, \"The menu is not the meal.\"", "Alan Watts, một triết gia phương Đông tài năng, diễn đạt lại sinh động hơn: \"Thực đơn không phải là bữa ăn.\""], [131.8, "Belief in the traditional sense, or certitude, or dogma, amounts to the grandiose delusion, \"My current model contains the whole universe and will never need to be revised.\"", "Niềm tin theo nghĩa truyền thống, hay sự chắc chắn, hay giáo điều, chẳng khác gì ảo tưởng vĩ đại: \"Mô hình hiện tại của tôi chứa cả vũ trụ và sẽ không bao giờ cần sửa đổi.\""], [145.8, "In terms of the history of science and knowledge in general, this appears absurd and arrogant to me, and I am perpetually astonished that so many people still manage to live with such a medieval attitude.", "Xét theo lịch sử khoa học và tri thức nói chung, với tôi điều này thật vô lý và kiêu ngạo, và tôi luôn kinh ngạc vì vẫn có rất nhiều người sống được với thái độ trung cổ như vậy."], [160.5, "Briefly, the main thing I have learned in my life is that reality is always plural and mutable.", "Nói ngắn gọn, điều chính tôi học được trong đời là thực tại luôn đa dạng và biến đổi."], [168.0, "Reality is a word in the English language which is (a) a noun and (b) singular.", "\"Reality\" (thực tại) là một từ trong tiếng Anh vừa (a) là danh từ, vừa (b) ở dạng số ít."], [175.2, "Thinking in the English language, and in many Indo-European languages, therefore subliminally programs us to imagine reality as one entity, sort of like a huge New York skyscraper in which every part is just another room within the same building.", "Vì thế, việc suy nghĩ bằng tiếng Anh và nhiều ngôn ngữ Ấn-Âu khác ngấm ngầm lập trình cho ta hình dung thực tại như một thực thể duy nhất, giống như một tòa nhà chọc trời khổng lồ ở New York, nơi mọi phần chỉ là một căn phòng khác trong cùng một tòa nhà."], [193.2, "This linguistic program is so pervasive that most people cannot think outside it at all, and when one tries to offer a different perspective, they imagine one is talking gibberish.", "Sự lập trình ngôn ngữ này phổ biến đến mức hầu hết mọi người hoàn toàn không thể nghĩ ra ngoài nó, và khi ai đó đưa ra một góc nhìn khác, họ tưởng người đó đang nói nhảm."], [206.1, "The notion that reality is a noun, a solid thing like a brick or a baseball bat, derives from the biological fact that our nervous systems normally organize the dance of energy into such block-like things, probably as instant survival cues.", "Quan niệm cho rằng thực tại là một danh từ, một vật rắn như viên gạch hay cây gậy bóng chày, bắt nguồn từ thực tế sinh học là hệ thần kinh của ta thường sắp xếp vũ điệu của năng lượng thành những khối như vậy, có lẽ như những tín hiệu sinh tồn tức thời."], [224.3, "Such things, however, dissolve back into energy dances, processes, or verbs, when the nervous system is joined with certain drugs, or transmuted by spiritual exercises, or aided by scientific instruments.", "Tuy nhiên, những thứ như vậy lại tan trở lại thành vũ điệu năng lượng, thành quá trình, hay động từ, khi hệ thần kinh chịu tác động của một số chất, hoặc được biến đổi qua các bài tập tâm linh, hoặc được hỗ trợ bởi thiết bị khoa học."], [238.9, "In both mysticism and physics, there is a general agreement that things are constructed by our nervous systems, and that realities, plural, are better described as systems, or bundles of energy functions.", "Cả trong thuyết thần bí lẫn vật lý, người ta nhìn chung đồng ý rằng mọi vật được hệ thần kinh của ta dựng nên, và rằng các thực tại, ở số nhiều, nên được mô tả như những hệ thống, hay những bó chức năng năng lượng."], [254.4, "So much for reality as a noun.", "Đó là chuyện thực tại như một danh từ."], [257.4, "The notion that reality is singular, like a sealed jar, does not jibe with current scientific findings, which, in this century, suggest that reality may better be considered as flowing and meandering like a river, or interacting like a dance, or evolving like life itself.", "Quan niệm cho rằng thực tại là số ít, như một cái lọ đậy kín, không khớp với các phát hiện khoa học hiện nay, vốn trong thế kỷ này cho thấy thực tại nên được coi là thứ chảy trôi và uốn lượn như dòng sông, tương tác như một điệu nhảy, hay tiến hóa như chính sự sống."], [279.1, "Most philosophers have known, at least since around 500 BC, that the world perceived by our senses is not the real world, but a construct we create, our own private work of art.", "Hầu hết các triết gia, ít nhất từ khoảng năm 500 trước Công nguyên, đã biết rằng thế giới mà giác quan ta cảm nhận không phải là thế giới thật, mà là một cấu trúc do ta tạo ra, một tác phẩm nghệ thuật riêng của mỗi người."], [293.0, "Modern science, beginning with Galileo's demonstration that color is not in objects but in the interaction of our senses with the object, understands that reality is created by our own brains.", "Khoa học hiện đại, bắt đầu từ việc Galileo chứng minh rằng màu sắc không nằm trong đồ vật mà nằm trong sự tương tác giữa giác quan với đồ vật, hiểu rằng thực tại được tạo ra bởi chính bộ não của chúng ta."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.4, "s", "Okay, let's get started with the mini-story lesson for the No Belief article."], [6.8, "s", "Here we go."], [7.3, "s", "First, just listen to the story."], [10.2, "s", "Once, there was a guy named Zed."], [13.1, "s", "Zed fervently believed he was better than everyone else."], [18.7, "s", "He knew with certitude that he was the smartest and best person in the world."], [25.6, "s", "He had a grandiose view of himself."], [31.0, "s", "This idea was immutable."], [34.3, "s", "One day,"], [35.5, "s", "Zed's friend Shannon meandered up to him and said to him,"], [40.7, "s", "Your ideas about yourself don't jibe with reality."], [44.6, "s", "You failed high school, you're ugly, and everybody hates you, except me."], [51.4, "s", "Shannon tried to provoke Zed with these words."], [54.6, "s", "She hoped to transmute his dogmatic belief into kindness and understanding."], [64.1, "s", "But Zed ignored her."], [66.2, "s", "He said, I failed high school because I was smarter than the teachers and they hated me."], [72.9, "s", "And you were just jealous that I'm better than you and everyone loves me."], [78.8, "s", "Shannon was incredulous."], [80.1, "s", "She couldn't believe Zed was so foolish and stupid."], [85.7, "s", "So much for reality, she said, and walked away."], [91.6, "s", "Okay, now let's listen again."], [93.7, "s", "I will ask questions to help you understand the new vocabulary better."], [100.9, "s", "You can use your pause button after I ask a question."], [104.7, "s", "Pause, because I ask the questions very quickly."], [107.3, "s", "So, if you need to pause, go ahead, pause and answer the question in your head, or you can say it out loud if you want to."], [114.9, "s", "Okay, here we go."], [116.7, "s", "Once there was a guy named Zed, Zed fervently believed he was better than everyone else."], [125.1, "s", "Was this a weak belief that Zed had?"], [128.4, "q", "Did he believe it just a little bit?"], [130.8, "a", "No, of course not."], [132.2, "s", "He fervently believed he was better."], [134.9, "q", "Did he strongly believe he was better?"], [138.7, "a", "Yes, he did."], [140.1, "s", "He strongly, he fervently believed he was better."], [145.5, "s", "Did he fervently believe he was better?"], [148.3, "q", "Or did he believe just a little bit, weakly, did he weakly believe?"], [153.6, "a", "Well, of course, he fervently believed he was better."], [157.1, "s", "He strongly believed he was better."], [160.9, "s", "How was his belief?"], [162.8, "q", "Was it a weak belief?"], [165.8, "a", "No, it was a fervent belief."], [168.1, "s", "He fervently believed he was better than everyone else."], [172.6, "s", "In fact, he knew with certitude that he was the smartest and the best man in the world."], [181.2, "q", "Did he have doubt about his belief?"], [185.0, "a", "No doubt."], [186.1, "s", "He believed with total certitude, he was completely sure."], [190.9, "q", "Did he have any doubt at all?"], [194.7, "a", "No, he believed with total certitude, he was completely sure."], [200.1, "s", "How did he believe?"], [202.3, "q", "Did he believe just a little bit?"], [206.1, "a", "No, he believed totally, completely, 100%."], [209.3, "s", "He was sure, he had total certitude that he was the smartest and the best person in the world."], [219.6, "q", "Was this a true view of himself?"], [224.1, "a", "No, no."], [225.3, "s", "He had a grandiose view of himself."], [228.4, "s", "Was his view of himself too big?"], [232.0, "q", "Too much?"], [233.6, "a", "Yes, that's right."], [234.6, "s", "It was too much."], [235.4, "s", "It was a grandiose view of himself."], [239.2, "s", "Did he have a humble view of himself?"], [242.0, "q", "Was he quiet and humble?"], [244.0, "a", "No."], [244.4, "s", "No, he had a grandiose view of himself, a very big, dramatic view of himself."], [250.9, "s", "He had a grandiose view of himself."], [254.4, "q", "Did his friend have a grandiose view of herself?"], [259.9, "a", "Well, I don't know, but no, I don't think so."], [262.2, "s", "No, she didn't."], [263.6, "s", "He, Zed, had a grandiose view of himself."], [267.2, "s", "But Shannon did not."], [268.6, "s", "Shannon was okay."], [269.6, "s", "She was normal."], [270.1, "s", "But she knew that Zed's view was grandiose."], [275.6, "s", "Was Zed's idea his belief in himself?"], [280.0, "q", "Was it changeable?"], [282.1, "a", "No."], [283.1, "s", "This idea was unmutable."], [285.7, "s", "Was unmutable could not be changed."], [288.9, "q", "Could this idea be changed?"], [290.5, "a", "No it could not."], [291.7, "q", "Why not?"], [293.0, "a", "Because it was unmutable."], [295.9, "s", "Was his idea mutable?"], [297.8, "q", "Or unmutable?"], [301.5, "a", "Well, it was unmutable, not changeable."], [305.6, "q", "Could Shannon change his idea?"], [308.4, "a", "No, she couldn't, because his idea about himself was unmutable, could not be changed."], [314.6, "s", "Still, Shannon tried."], [316.2, "s", "One day."], [317.3, "s", "His friend Shannon meandered up to him and said."], [321.2, "s", "Your ideas about yourself don't jive with reality."], [325.3, "s", "Did she walk directly ugly to him, very fast."], [329.2, "s", "No, she meandered up to him."], [332.4, "q", "Did she run up to him?"], [334.8, "a", "No, she did not."], [336.2, "s", "She meandered up to him."], [338.6, "q", "Who meandered up to Zed?"], [342.4, "a", "Well, Shannon meandered up to Zed."], [345.9, "q", "Did she walk slowly, maybe not in a straight line, kind of slowly come up to him?"], [353.1, "a", "Yeah that's right."], [354.1, "s", "That's exactly what she did."], [355.5, "s", "She meandered up to him."], [357.1, "s", "She slowly kind of walked up to him, maybe stopping a little, going to the left, going to the right."], [362.7, "s", "And finally she comes to him."], [364.1, "s", "She meandered up to him after she meandered up to him."], [367.9, "q", "What did she say?"], [369.8, "a", "Well, she said, your ideas about yourself don't jibe with reality."], [376.7, "q", "Did his ideas with reality, did his ideas about himself, I'm sorry, jibe with reality?"], [382.4, "a", "No they did not."], [384.2, "q", "Did they agree with reality?"], [387.0, "a", "No."], [387.9, "s", "His idea and reality were totally different."], [391.7, "s", "His ideas about himself and reality did not jibe, right?"], [396.9, "s", "His ideas did not jibe with reality."], [401.5, "q", "Did Shannon's ideas, did her ideas jibe with reality?"], [407.0, "a", "Yes, they did."], [408.2, "s", "Her ideas did jibe with reality."], [411.4, "s", "She said, Oh, you failed high school, you're ugly, and everybody hates you."], [416.6, "s", "Unfortunately, this is true."], [418.3, "s", "Zed really was ugly, and he really did fail high school, and everyone really did hate him except for Shannon."], [424.8, "s", "So Shannon's view did jibe with reality, but Zed's view of himself did not jibe with reality."], [432.7, "s", "So Shannon tried to provoke Zed with these words?"], [438.3, "q", "Did she try to provoke him with kindness?"], [442.1, "a", "No, she didn't try to provoke him with kindness."], [444.8, "q", "Did she try to provoke him with tough words, hard words?"], [450.9, "a", "Yes, that's right."], [452.1, "s", "Shannon tried to provoke him with hard, tough words."], [456.2, "s", "Did she want to get a strong reaction?"], [459.2, "q", "Did she want a strong reaction from Zed?"], [462.4, "a", "Yes, that's right."], [463.2, "s", "She tried to provoke him."], [464.7, "s", "She wanted him to react."], [466.5, "s", "She wanted him to change his mind."], [469.1, "q", "Did she try to provoke her mother?"], [473.9, "a", "Oh, no, of course not."], [475.8, "q", "Who did she try to provoke?"], [479.1, "a", "She tried to provoke Zed."], [481.8, "s", "She tried to provoke Zed, her friend."], [484.6, "s", "Okay."], [485.4, "s", "And why?"], [486.5, "q", "Why did she try to provoke Zed?"], [489.8, "a", "Well, she hoped to transmute his dogmatic belief into kindness and understanding."], [497.6, "s", "She wanted him to become kind and understanding."], [502.4, "q", "Did she want to change his strong belief into kindness?"], [508.6, "a", "That's right."], [509.2, "s", "Yes, she did."], [510.1, "s", "She wanted to transmute his belief, I'm the best, into kindness."], [515.8, "s", "Oh, I want to help people."], [517.0, "s", "Right?"], [517.9, "s", "She wanted to transmute his strong belief into kindness."], [522.0, "s", "Did she want to transmute his appearance?"], [524.3, "q", "How he looked?"], [526.3, "a", "No, she didn't care about that."], [527.9, "s", "She didn't want to transmute his appearance."], [531.1, "s", "Did she want to transmute his intelligence?"], [534.8, "q", "Change his intelligence?"], [536.2, "a", "No, no."], [537.3, "s", "She didn't care about his intelligence."], [538.6, "s", "She didn't want to change."], [539.8, "s", "She didn't want to transmute his intelligence into kindness."], [543.7, "q", "What did she want to transmute?"], [546.8, "a", "She wanted to transmute his belief."], [550.0, "s", "What kind of belief was it?"], [552.5, "q", "Was it a flexible belief?"], [555.2, "a", "No, not a flexible belief."], [557.1, "s", "It was a dogmatic belief."], [559.8, "s", "Very strong, total faith in this belief."], [562.9, "s", "It is correct."], [564.2, "s", "It is always correct."], [565.4, "s", "I am right."], [566.4, "s", "Everyone else is wrong."], [567.4, "s", "That's a dogmatic belief."], [570.2, "q", "Was his belief about himself dogmatic?"], [574.8, "a", "Yes, it was."], [576.0, "s", "It was a dogmatic belief."], [578.4, "q", "Did he dogmatically believe he was the best?"], [582.9, "a", "Yes, that's correct."], [584.0, "s", "He dogmatically believed he was the best."], [588.0, "q", "Did he have a dogmatic religious belief?"], [591.8, "a", "No."], [592.6, "q", "He didn't have dogmatic religious belief?"], [594.5, "a", "He wasn't religious."], [596.0, "q", "Did he have a dogmatic scientific belief?"], [600.0, "a", "No, no."], [601.0, "s", "He didn't care about science."], [602.3, "s", "He didn't have a dogmatic scientific belief."], [604.9, "q", "What kind of dogmatic belief did he have?"], [608.2, "a", "Well, he had a dogmatic belief about himself."], [611.9, "s", "He thought he was the best."], [614.8, "s", "Did Zed listen to Shannon's words?"], [618.2, "s", "Was he provoked?"], [619.9, "s", "Did he change?"], [621.0, "q", "Did he?"], [626.1, "a", "He said, I failed high school because I was smarter than the teachers and they hated me."], [632.1, "s", "And you, Shannon, you're just jealous that I'm better than you and everybody loves me."], [639.0, "s", "How did Shannon feel when she heard these words?"], [642.0, "q", "Was she surprised?"], [644.0, "a", "Yes, she was surprised."], [645.4, "s", "She was incredulous."], [647.0, "s", "Very surprised."], [648.8, "q", "Was she angry?"], [650.2, "a", "No."], [651.2, "s", "She was incredulous, she was surprised."], [654.2, "q", "Was she sad?"], [655.9, "a", "No, she wasn't sad, she was incredulous."], [658.5, "s", "She was very surprised, shocked."], [662.4, "q", "Was she incredulous about his looks, because he was ugly?"], [667.6, "a", "No, she knew he was ugly."], [669.6, "s", "She was not incredulous about his looks."], [672.4, "q", "Was she incredulous about his clothes, how he dressed?"], [676.6, "a", "No, she wasn't incredulous, she wasn't surprised about his clothes."], [679.2, "q", "What was she incredulous about?"], [683.6, "a", "She was incredulous about his words, his reaction."], [687.3, "s", "He said, oh, I'm the best."], [688.8, "s", "Everyone's jealous."], [689.9, "s", "And you are jealous."], [691.8, "s", "She was stunned."], [692.7, "s", "She was shocked."], [693.4, "s", "She was incredulous."], [695.1, "s", "She couldn't believe Zed was so foolish and stupid."], [700.4, "s", "So she says, so much for reality."], [704.3, "s", "And then she walked away."], [706.3, "q", "Did she want to continue talking about reality?"], [711.9, "a", "No."], [712.6, "s", "She was finished with that subject."], [714.6, "s", "She said, so much for reality."], [717.2, "s", "So much for, meaning I'm finished talking about this."], [720.0, "s", "The topic is over."], [721.4, "s", "So much for reality, she said, and she walked away."], [724.7, "q", "Did she say, so much for money?"], [727.7, "a", "No, she did not."], [728.5, "s", "She said, so much for reality."], [730.1, "s", "Did she want to talk about books?"], [732.6, "q", "Did she want to stop talking about books?"], [735.8, "a", "No, she wanted to stop talking about reality."], [739.3, "q", "What did she want to stop talking about?"], [742.4, "a", "Well, she said, so much for reality."], [745.4, "s", "Enough of talking about reality."], [748.0, "s", "So much for the topic of reality."], [750.0, "s", "I'm done with the topic of reality."], [752.9, "s", "And then she walked away."], [756.2, "s", "Okay, very good."], [757.9, "s", "Next I'm going to read it again this time."], [760.5, "s", "I'm going to pause, I'm going to repeat a few of the key phrases with the new words."], [766.7, "s", "And I'll pause a little bit."], [769.1, "s", "And please repeat the phrase out loud."], [771.7, "s", "Repeat it again."], [772.8, "s", "Copy my pronunciation."], [774.4, "s", "Copy my pauses."], [775.9, "s", "Copy when I go up and when I go down."], [779.4, "s", "Copy when I'm loud and when I'm soft."], [781.9, "s", "Copy my pronunciation exactly."], [784.6, "s", "If you need to pause with your iPod, use the pause button."], [788.4, "s", "It's okay."], [788.7, "s", "Okay, here we go."], [790.3, "s", "Once there was a guy named Zed, Zed fervently believed he was better than everyone."], [797.3, "s", "Zed fervently believed he was better than everyone."], [805.7, "s", "Good."], [806.5, "s", "He knew with certitude that he was the best."], [812.1, "s", "He knew with certitude that he was the best."], [819.1, "s", "He had a grandiose view of himself."], [825.5, "s", "Good."], [825.7, "s", "But he had a grandiose view of himself."], [831.5, "s", "This idea was unmutable."], [837.0, "s", "This idea was unmutable."], [841.1, "s", "One day, Zed's friend Shannon meandered up to him."], [847.5, "s", "One day, Zed's friend Shannon meandered up to him."], [853.6, "s", "She said, your ideas don't jibe with reality."], [860.5, "s", "She said, your ideas don't jibe with reality."], [868.3, "s", "Good."], [868.9, "s", "You failed high school, you're ugly, and everyone hates you."], [872.4, "s", "Shannon tried to provoke Zed."], [877.2, "s", "Good."], [877.9, "s", "Shannon tried to provoke Zed."], [883.6, "s", "She hoped to transmute his dogmatic belief into kindness."], [893.1, "s", "She hoped to transmute his dogmatic belief into kindness."], [902.1, "s", "Good."], [902.4, "s", "But Zed ignored her."], [904.4, "s", "He said, I failed high school because I was smarter than the teachers and they hated me and you're just jealous."], [910.9, "s", "Shannon was incredulous."], [916.6, "s", "Shannon was incredulous."], [922.4, "s", "She couldn't believe Zed was so foolish and stupid."], [925.6, "s", "So much for reality, she said."], [931.2, "s", "So much for reality, she said."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"label": "", "audio": "Original_Course/124c No Belief (ms).mp3", "story": [[0.4, "s", "Okay, let's get started with the mini-story lesson for the No Belief article."], [6.8, "s", "Here we go."], [7.3, "s", "First, just listen to the story."], [10.2, "s", "Once, there was a guy named Zed."], [13.1, "s", "Zed fervently believed he was better than everyone else."], [18.7, "s", "He knew with certitude that he was the smartest and best person in the world."], [25.6, "s", "He had a grandiose view of himself."], [31.0, "s", "This idea was immutable."], [34.3, "s", "One day,"], [35.5, "s", "Zed's friend Shannon meandered up to him and said to him,"], [40.7, "s", "Your ideas about yourself don't jibe with reality."], [44.6, "s", "You failed high school, you're ugly, and everybody hates you, except me."], [51.4, "s", "Shannon tried to provoke Zed with these words."], [54.6, "s", "She hoped to transmute his dogmatic belief into kindness and understanding."], [64.1, "s", "But Zed ignored her."], [66.2, "s", "He said, I failed high school because I was smarter than the teachers and they hated me."], [72.9, "s", "And you were just jealous that I'm better than you and everyone loves me."], [78.8, "s", "Shannon was incredulous."], [80.1, "s", "She couldn't believe Zed was so foolish and stupid."], [85.7, "s", "So much for reality, she said, and walked away."], [91.6, "s", "Okay, now let's listen again."], [93.7, "s", "I will ask questions to help you understand the new vocabulary better."], [100.9, "s", "You can use your pause button after I ask a question."], [104.7, "s", "Pause, because I ask the questions very quickly."], [107.3, "s", "So, if you need to pause, go ahead, pause and answer the question in your head, or you can say it out loud if you want to."], [114.9, "s", "Okay, here we go."], [116.7, "s", "Once there was a guy named Zed, Zed fervently believed he was better than everyone else."], [125.1, "s", "Was this a weak belief that Zed had?"], [128.4, "q", "Did he believe it just a little bit?"], [130.8, "a", "No, of course not."], [132.2, "s", "He fervently believed he was better."], [134.9, "q", "Did he strongly believe he was better?"], [138.7, "a", "Yes, he did."], [140.1, "s", "He strongly, he fervently believed he was better."], [145.5, "s", "Did he fervently believe he was better?"], [148.3, "q", "Or did he believe just a little bit, weakly, did he weakly believe?"], [153.6, "a", "Well, of course, he fervently believed he was better."], [157.1, "s", "He strongly believed he was better."], [160.9, "s", "How was his belief?"], [162.8, "q", "Was it a weak belief?"], [165.8, "a", "No, it was a fervent belief."], [168.1, "s", "He fervently believed he was better than everyone else."], [172.6, "s", "In fact, he knew with certitude that he was the smartest and the best man in the world."], [181.2, "q", "Did he have doubt about his belief?"], [185.0, "a", "No doubt."], [186.1, "s", "He believed with total certitude, he was completely sure."], [190.9, "q", "Did he have any doubt at all?"], [194.7, "a", "No, he believed with total certitude, he was completely sure."], [200.1, "s", "How did he believe?"], [202.3, "q", "Did he believe just a little bit?"], [206.1, "a", "No, he believed totally, completely, 100%."], [209.3, "s", "He was sure, he had total certitude that he was the smartest and the best person in the world."], [219.6, "q", "Was this a true view of himself?"], [224.1, "a", "No, no."], [225.3, "s", "He had a grandiose view of himself."], [228.4, "s", "Was his view of himself too big?"], [232.0, "q", "Too much?"], [233.6, "a", "Yes, that's right."], [234.6, "s", "It was too much."], [235.4, "s", "It was a grandiose view of himself."], [239.2, "s", "Did he have a humble view of himself?"], [242.0, "q", "Was he quiet and humble?"], [244.0, "a", "No."], [244.4, "s", "No, he had a grandiose view of himself, a very big, dramatic view of himself."], [250.9, "s", "He had a grandiose view of himself."], [254.4, "q", "Did his friend have a grandiose view of herself?"], [259.9, "a", "Well, I don't know, but no, I don't think so."], [262.2, "s", "No, she didn't."], [263.6, "s", "He, Zed, had a grandiose view of himself."], [267.2, "s", "But Shannon did not."], [268.6, "s", "Shannon was okay."], [269.6, "s", "She was normal."], [270.1, "s", "But she knew that Zed's view was grandiose."], [275.6, "s", "Was Zed's idea his belief in himself?"], [280.0, "q", "Was it changeable?"], [282.1, "a", "No."], [283.1, "s", "This idea was unmutable."], [285.7, "s", "Was unmutable could not be changed."], [288.9, "q", "Could this idea be changed?"], [290.5, "a", "No it could not."], [291.7, "q", "Why not?"], [293.0, "a", "Because it was unmutable."], [295.9, "s", "Was his idea mutable?"], [297.8, "q", "Or unmutable?"], [301.5, "a", "Well, it was unmutable, not changeable."], [305.6, "q", "Could Shannon change his idea?"], [308.4, "a", "No, she couldn't, because his idea about himself was unmutable, could not be changed."], [314.6, "s", "Still, Shannon tried."], [316.2, "s", "One day."], [317.3, "s", "His friend Shannon meandered up to him and said."], [321.2, "s", "Your ideas about yourself don't jive with reality."], [325.3, "s", "Did she walk directly ugly to him, very fast."], [329.2, "s", "No, she meandered up to him."], [332.4, "q", "Did she run up to him?"], [334.8, "a", "No, she did not."], [336.2, "s", "She meandered up to him."], [338.6, "q", "Who meandered up to Zed?"], [342.4, "a", "Well, Shannon meandered up to Zed."], [345.9, "q", "Did she walk slowly, maybe not in a straight line, kind of slowly come up to him?"], [353.1, "a", "Yeah that's right."], [354.1, "s", "That's exactly what she did."], [355.5, "s", "She meandered up to him."], [357.1, "s", "She slowly kind of walked up to him, maybe stopping a little, going to the left, going to the right."], [362.7, "s", "And finally she comes to him."], [364.1, "s", "She meandered up to him after she meandered up to him."], [367.9, "q", "What did she say?"], [369.8, "a", "Well, she said, your ideas about yourself don't jibe with reality."], [376.7, "q", "Did his ideas with reality, did his ideas about himself, I'm sorry, jibe with reality?"], [382.4, "a", "No they did not."], [384.2, "q", "Did they agree with reality?"], [387.0, "a", "No."], [387.9, "s", "His idea and reality were totally different."], [391.7, "s", "His ideas about himself and reality did not jibe, right?"], [396.9, "s", "His ideas did not jibe with reality."], [401.5, "q", "Did Shannon's ideas, did her ideas jibe with reality?"], [407.0, "a", "Yes, they did."], [408.2, "s", "Her ideas did jibe with reality."], [411.4, "s", "She said, Oh, you failed high school, you're ugly, and everybody hates you."], [416.6, "s", "Unfortunately, this is true."], [418.3, "s", "Zed really was ugly, and he really did fail high school, and everyone really did hate him except for Shannon."], [424.8, "s", "So Shannon's view did jibe with reality, but Zed's view of himself did not jibe with reality."], [432.7, "s", "So Shannon tried to provoke Zed with these words?"], [438.3, "q", "Did she try to provoke him with kindness?"], [442.1, "a", "No, she didn't try to provoke him with kindness."], [444.8, "q", "Did she try to provoke him with tough words, hard words?"], [450.9, "a", "Yes, that's right."], [452.1, "s", "Shannon tried to provoke him with hard, tough words."], [456.2, "s", "Did she want to get a strong reaction?"], [459.2, "q", "Did she want a strong reaction from Zed?"], [462.4, "a", "Yes, that's right."], [463.2, "s", "She tried to provoke him."], [464.7, "s", "She wanted him to react."], [466.5, "s", "She wanted him to change his mind."], [469.1, "q", "Did she try to provoke her mother?"], [473.9, "a", "Oh, no, of course not."], [475.8, "q", "Who did she try to provoke?"], [479.1, "a", "She tried to provoke Zed."], [481.8, "s", "She tried to provoke Zed, her friend."], [484.6, "s", "Okay."], [485.4, "s", "And why?"], [486.5, "q", "Why did she try to provoke Zed?"], [489.8, "a", "Well, she hoped to transmute his dogmatic belief into kindness and understanding."], [497.6, "s", "She wanted him to become kind and understanding."], [502.4, "q", "Did she want to change his strong belief into kindness?"], [508.6, "a", "That's right."], [509.2, "s", "Yes, she did."], [510.1, "s", "She wanted to transmute his belief, I'm the best, into kindness."], [515.8, "s", "Oh, I want to help people."], [517.0, "s", "Right?"], [517.9, "s", "She wanted to transmute his strong belief into kindness."], [522.0, "s", "Did she want to transmute his appearance?"], [524.3, "q", "How he looked?"], [526.3, "a", "No, she didn't care about that."], [527.9, "s", "She didn't want to transmute his appearance."], [531.1, "s", "Did she want to transmute his intelligence?"], [534.8, "q", "Change his intelligence?"], [536.2, "a", "No, no."], [537.3, "s", "She didn't care about his intelligence."], [538.6, "s", "She didn't want to change."], [539.8, "s", "She didn't want to transmute his intelligence into kindness."], [543.7, "q", "What did she want to transmute?"], [546.8, "a", "She wanted to transmute his belief."], [550.0, "s", "What kind of belief was it?"], [552.5, "q", "Was it a flexible belief?"], [555.2, "a", "No, not a flexible belief."], [557.1, "s", "It was a dogmatic belief."], [559.8, "s", "Very strong, total faith in this belief."], [562.9, "s", "It is correct."], [564.2, "s", "It is always correct."], [565.4, "s", "I am right."], [566.4, "s", "Everyone else is wrong."], [567.4, "s", "That's a dogmatic belief."], [570.2, "q", "Was his belief about himself dogmatic?"], [574.8, "a", "Yes, it was."], [576.0, "s", "It was a dogmatic belief."], [578.4, "q", "Did he dogmatically believe he was the best?"], [582.9, "a", "Yes, that's correct."], [584.0, "s", "He dogmatically believed he was the best."], [588.0, "q", "Did he have a dogmatic religious belief?"], [591.8, "a", "No."], [592.6, "q", "He didn't have dogmatic religious belief?"], [594.5, "a", "He wasn't religious."], [596.0, "q", "Did he have a dogmatic scientific belief?"], [600.0, "a", "No, no."], [601.0, "s", "He didn't care about science."], [602.3, "s", "He didn't have a dogmatic scientific belief."], [604.9, "q", "What kind of dogmatic belief did he have?"], [608.2, "a", "Well, he had a dogmatic belief about himself."], [611.9, "s", "He thought he was the best."], [614.8, "s", "Did Zed listen to Shannon's words?"], [618.2, "s", "Was he provoked?"], [619.9, "s", "Did he change?"], [621.0, "q", "Did he?"], [626.1, "a", "He said, I failed high school because I was smarter than the teachers and they hated me."], [632.1, "s", "And you, Shannon, you're just jealous that I'm better than you and everybody loves me."], [639.0, "s", "How did Shannon feel when she heard these words?"], [642.0, "q", "Was she surprised?"], [644.0, "a", "Yes, she was surprised."], [645.4, "s", "She was incredulous."], [647.0, "s", "Very surprised."], [648.8, "q", "Was she angry?"], [650.2, "a", "No."], [651.2, "s", "She was incredulous, she was surprised."], [654.2, "q", "Was she sad?"], [655.9, "a", "No, she wasn't sad, she was incredulous."], [658.5, "s", "She was very surprised, shocked."], [662.4, "q", "Was she incredulous about his looks, because he was ugly?"], [667.6, "a", "No, she knew he was ugly."], [669.6, "s", "She was not incredulous about his looks."], [672.4, "q", "Was she incredulous about his clothes, how he dressed?"], [676.6, "a", "No, she wasn't incredulous, she wasn't surprised about his clothes."], [679.2, "q", "What was she incredulous about?"], [683.6, "a", "She was incredulous about his words, his reaction."], [687.3, "s", "He said, oh, I'm the best."], [688.8, "s", "Everyone's jealous."], [689.9, "s", "And you are jealous."], [691.8, "s", "She was stunned."], [692.7, "s", "She was shocked."], [693.4, "s", "She was incredulous."], [695.1, "s", "She couldn't believe Zed was so foolish and stupid."], [700.4, "s", "So she says, so much for reality."], [7