  $j$[[0.5, "Okay, welcome to the commentary for the No Belief article and lessons."], [7.4, "I'm just going to chat about my ideas on this topic."], [12.1, "First of all, this comes from Robert Anton Wilson."], [16.2, "He's the guy who wrote the main article."], [19.0, "And Robert Anton Wilson is a very interesting guy."], [22.6, "Very interesting guy."], [24.8, "He's kind of a part philosopher, part activist, he's a writer."], [33.0, "Anyway, he's got a lot of interesting ideas."], [35.7, "I like him."], [36.4, "He likes to challenge the status quo."], [40.0, "Status quo meaning what is normal, what everyone believes."], [43.2, "He likes to challenge dogma."], [46.0, "People have so many strong beliefs, and he likes to challenge those beliefs."], [50.7, "So, that's why I like him, I guess I feel the same way."], [55.4, "And this little, I guess you would call it an essay, this little essay he wrote, called No Belief, or I Have No Beliefs, is very interesting."], [65.3, "And it basically discusses the danger of belief itself."], [70.7, "And here, what we're talking about is belief meaning you think something is correct."], [77.4, "And When you have this 100% idea."], [80.0, "This is definitely right and this is definitely wrong."], [85.0, "This is definitely true."], [86.6, "This is definitely false."], [88.4, "That's a belief, a strong belief, and I think he's really talking about strong belief."], [93.1, "I mean, we all have ideas."], [94.7, "We all have certain beliefs."], [96.8, "We think we know something, but what Robert Anton Wilson is talking about is we must always remember that we can never be 100% sure."], [105.7, "We might be 90% sure, we might be 40% sure, but never 100%."], [112.5, "There is no definite reality where we can always say, we know for sure."], [119.8, "Absolutely."], [121.1, "And I like that, and I think he's absolutely correct."], [124.8, "And his idea, I think, is appropriate."], [129.0, "Can be applied at a very large level, a very deep level, and also at a kind of very small practical level."], [135.8, "At a big, deep level, what he's talking about in terms of reality."], [140.4, "Are these questions of religion and philosophy and science."], [145.2, "What is real?"], [147.4, "What is life?"], [149.9, "That's a very deep question."], [152.5, "And he talks about this idea that in the past."], [156.5, "Especially he refers to European thought, that this medieval period, people believe that the world was made of things."], [166.5, "Solid things."], [168.4, "And of course, our normal reality, that's what we see."], [172.5, "You pick up a pen, it seems like a nice, hard thing."], [176.6, "And then you have a desk, it's a hard, solid thing."], [180.3, "And the idea is that all of reality is these little blocks, these little pieces of hard things."], [187.1, "And that was a view in the Western world for many years."], [193.6, "Until science, especially physics, began to question that belief, question that idea."], [202.7, "And physics, as physicists."], [204.8, "Began to explore the atom."], [206.8, "And they went even farther, smaller and smaller and smaller."], [211.1, "Physics began to realize, uh oh, it's not true."], [214.2, "The world, reality, things appear like they're hard and solid, but in fact they are made of energy."], [223.9, "They're made of moving processes."], [227.6, "They're made of things that are not solid."], [231.0, "Things that change constantly, that are flowing, that are moving."], [235.7, "Electrons and magnetic energy and all these things."], [239.8, "And that this idea of solid separate things is something that our mind creates, that our senses and our mind."], [247.7, "Our senses meaning our eyes, our ears, our nose, and then of course our brains also."], [253.1, "That we take all this information, all these waves, all this energy, all these patterns."], [260.8, "And we make them with our minds into separate items."], [265.7, "But in fact, nothing is actually separate."], [267.7, "What's interesting, and what he talks about, is how this idea of science,"], [274.7, "of especially advanced science, agrees with mysticism."], [280.7, "And mysticism is a word, it can have a lot of different feelings depending on who's using it."], [286.4, "But mysticism basically means direct religion."], [290.0, "Religion based on observation, religious based on meditation."], [294.3, "So, a religion that is not based on belief or some dogmatic rules or a book."], [303.0, "So, Buddhism, for example, is kind of a mystical religion."], [307.2, "It's based on meditation and observation."], [310.6, "Hinduism, to a large part, is at least parts of Hinduism."], [314.1, "And it's interesting, so he's saying, and parts of Christianity too, as a matter of fact."], [317.3, "So anyway."], [318.6, "These mystic, these mystical as the adjective, these mystical religions or religious sex, religious groups."], [326.0, "In fact agree, their understanding."], [329.8, "Their ideas, agree with the physicist ideas."], [333.8, "And that is that, in fact, everything changes and nothing is solid and separate."], [341.1, "Quite interesting."], [341.8, "So that's at the big level, the big philosophical, religious, spiritual level."], [347.7, "This idea of dogma, strong belief, right?"], [351.1, "And of course we see the negative effects of dogma in politics in the world all the time."], [357.4, "We have dogmatic Christians who believe the Bible is the word of God and God wrote it."], [363.5, "And it's 100% absolutely true, exactly true, and nothing else is."], [369.4, "And therefore it's okay to kill other people who don't believe it or at least condemn them and attack them."], [377.0, "So that's a dogmatic belief, right?"], [379.3, "The Bible is 100% right, everyone else is 100% wrong."], [383.5, "And this dogma, these dogmatic beliefs cause a lot of problems in the world and in personal relationships too."], [391.5, "But at a smaller level, at a smaller level, in our own lives."], [396.4, "This idea is also important, I think, in my own life it is, that we have to remind ourselves all the time that our beliefs are not sure."], [406.9, "We can never be totally sure."], [408.6, "I have strong ideas, for example, about teaching English."], [411.9, "I have very strong ideas."], [413.4, "what I think is correct, what I think works,"], [417.0, "what I think is the best way to do it, and what I think is not."], [421.6, "Now, these ideas, they're not random."], [424.2, "I've read a lot of research."], [426.2, "I have a master's degree in teaching English as a foreign language, and I had to read a lot of lots and lots and lots of research studies."], [434.4, "I also have ten years of experience, so I've seen a lot of students."], [438.5, "I've examined how they learn, how they study, which students learn faster, which ones do better."], [445.7, "So I have reasons for my beliefs."], [447.9, "However, I have to always remember that But I can't let this become a dogma."], [455.6, "I can't let myself have total certitude."], [460.4, "I have to remember that next week, next month, there might be new research, right?"], [465.9, "Someone might develop a new technique for teaching language, and maybe that technique will be better than the storytelling technique."], [474.5, "Maybe it will be better than what I do in my class or what we do at Effortless English."], [480.3, "And I need to be open; I need to remember that."], [484.4, "Because if someone creates a better method, well, I want to use that method, right?"], [490.1, "I don't want to be stuck with what I have now."], [494.2, "That's the idea of always being a little bit unsure."], [497.9, "It's okay to be unsure; in fact, it's very good to say, you know, I'm not totally sure."], [504.7, "So for myself, I try to remember that."], [507.7, "I also try to remember it in my general life, my personal life, with my friends, with my other relationships."], [515.2, "I think I'm right."], [516.7, "We all think we're right."], [518.2, "We all pretty sure I'm right, I know I'm right, but in fact, maybe we're wrong."], [523.5, "We should always remember there is a chance that we're wrong, or at least mistaken."], [531.8, "Alright."], [533.0, "And I think this comes down to finally that both at a large level, in terms of religion."], [539.3, "At our work and in our personal lives, we always need to question."], [544.3, "We always have to ask questions, we always have to be reflecting about our lives."], [549.7, "Am I doing what is best?"], [552.5, "Is what I'm doing now still working?"], [555.6, "Is there new information I could be using?"], [558.9, "Has the situation changed?"], [560.5, "Maybe what I did used to be the best, used to be good, but And maybe now the situation is different and I need to change."], [568.1, "So we always have to keep questioning, keep questioning."], [571.3, "Never be sure."], [572.5, "It's okay, I like this idea, to say, I have no strong beliefs."], [577.6, "I'm always a little bit unsure."], [580.1, "I never know 100%."], [582.2, "I never have total certitude."], [585.0, "That's how we grow."], [586.7, "That's how we remain creative."], [590.6, "That's how we keep getting better."], [592.8, "Keep innovating, keep succeeding with our lives, in all aspects of our lives."], [600.5, "So anyway, it's a nice idea."], [603.2, "I think Robert Anton Wilson says it much better than I do."], [606.8, "Hopefully I can say it with a little bit simpler English."], [610.1, "His article is a little bit difficult."], [612.3, "So if you had problems with his article, if it seems difficult, just relax, no problem."], [616.9, "Focus on the mini-story for a while."], [619.2, "And focus on reading it, and then start listening to the audio article and you know just repeat it."], [626.1, "The great thing about effortless English, you don't need to feel stress."], [630.3, "Anytime you have an article that is difficult for you just relax, just listen to it more."], [638.7, "That's a simple solution."], [640.9, "Sometimes you can understand an article completely after one week."], [646.5, "Sometimes you might need to listen to it every day for one month."], [652.5, "Sometimes you might need to, you know, forget about it for a while and come back, try it again after three months, after six months."], [661.3, "It's okay, no problem."], [662.8, "Focus on the lessons that are easiest for you, that are the best for you."], [667.8, "Sometimes you can do all of them."], [669.6, "Sometimes maybe focus on the mini-story."], [672.7, "Use what works for you."], [674.4, "This is your club so use what works for you."], [678.5, "Alrighty, I will see you next time, bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["belief", "/bɪˈliːf/", "niềm tin"], ["remark", "/rɪˈmɑːk/", "lời nhận xét"], ["debate", "/dɪˈbeɪt/", "cuộc tranh luận"], ["provoke", "/prəˈvəʊk/", "gây ra, khơi lên"], ["incredulity", "/ˌɪnkrəˈdjuːləti/", "sự hoài nghi, không tin"], ["hangover", "/ˈhæŋəʊvə/", "tàn dư, di chứng"], ["medieval", "/ˌmediˈiːvl/", "thời trung cổ"], ["theist", "/ˈθiːɪst/", "người hữu thần"], ["dogmatic", "/dɒɡˈmætɪk/", "giáo điều"], ["atheist", "/ˈeɪθiɪst/", "người vô thần"], ["fervently", "/ˈfɜːvəntli/", "nhiệt thành"], ["blind faith", "/blaɪnd feɪθ/", "niềm tin mù quáng"], ["reverse", "/rɪˈvɜːs/", "điều ngược lại"], ["doctrine", "/ˈdɒktrɪn/", "học thuyết"], ["certitude", "/ˈsɜːtɪtjuːd/", "sự chắc chắn"], ["clinically dead", "/ˈklɪnɪkli ded/", "chết lâm sàng"], ["identical", "/aɪˈdentɪkl/", "giống hệt"], ["formulate", "/ˈfɔːmjuleɪt/", "đưa ra, xây dựng"], ["agnosticism", "/æɡˈnɒstɪsɪzəm/", "thuyết bất khả tri"], ["territory", "/ˈterətri/", "lãnh thổ"], ["vividly", "/ˈvɪvɪdli/", "sinh động"], ["dogma", "/ˈdɒɡmə/", "giáo điều"], ["amount to", "/əˈmaʊnt tuː/", "chẳng khác gì, tương đương"], ["grandiose", "/ˈɡrændiəʊs/", "vĩ đại, phô trương"], ["delusion", "/dɪˈluːʒn/", "ảo tưởng"], ["absurd", "/əbˈsɜːd/", "vô lý"], ["arrogant", "/ˈærəɡənt/", "kiêu ngạo"], ["perpetually", "/pəˈpetʃuəli/", "mãi mãi, liên tục"], ["astonished", "/əˈstɒnɪʃt/", "kinh ngạc"], ["plural", "/ˈplʊərəl/", "số nhiều"], ["mutable", "/ˈmjuːtəbl/", "có thể thay đổi"], ["subliminally", "/sʌbˈlɪmɪnəli/", "một cách tiềm thức"], ["entity", "/ˈentəti/", "thực thể"], ["pervasive", "/pəˈveɪsɪv/", "lan tràn, phổ biến"], ["perspective", "/pəˈspektɪv/", "góc nhìn"], ["gibberish", "/ˈdʒɪbərɪʃ/", "lời nói nhảm"], ["derive from", "/dɪˈraɪv frɒm/", "bắt nguồn từ"], ["dissolve", "/dɪˈzɒlv/", "tan ra"], ["mysticism", "/ˈmɪstɪsɪzəm/", "thuyết thần bí"], ["jibe with", "/dʒaɪb wɪð/", "khớp với"], ["meander", "/miˈændə/", "uốn khúc"], ["construct", "/ˈkɒnstrʌkt/", "cấu trúc, sản phẩm tạo dựng"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["in these very words", "đúng từng chữ như vậy"], ["provoked incredulity on the part of most viewers", "khiến phần lớn khán giả không tin nổi"], ["a hangover of the medieval Catholic Church", "tàn dư của Giáo hội Công giáo trung cổ"], ["believe something or other", "tin vào điều gì đó"], ["believe fervently in socialism", "tin cuồng nhiệt vào chủ nghĩa xã hội"], ["blind faith", "niềm tin mù quáng"], ["belief is the death of intelligence", "niềm tin là cái chết của trí tuệ"], ["a doctrine of any sort", "bất kỳ học thuyết nào"], ["the less there is left to think about", "càng ít điều còn lại để suy nghĩ"], ["identical to that of Dr. Gribbin", "giống hệt với tiến sĩ Gribbin"], ["should not be confused with the world itself", "không nên nhầm với chính thế giới"], ["The map is not the territory.", "Bản đồ không phải là lãnh thổ."], ["The menu is not the meal.", "Thực đơn không phải là bữa ăn."], ["the grandiose delusion", "ảo tưởng vĩ đại"], ["absurd and arrogant", "vô lý và kiêu ngạo"], ["reality is always plural and mutable", "thực tại luôn đa dạng và biến đổi"], ["cannot think outside it at all", "hoàn toàn không thể nghĩ ra ngoài nó"], ["talking gibberish", "nói nhảm"], ["So much for", "Đó là chuyện về"], ["does not jibe with current scientific findings", "không khớp với phát hiện khoa học hiện nay"], ["our own private work of art", "tác phẩm nghệ thuật riêng của mỗi người"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["S + provoke(d) + noun + on the part of + someone", "His joke provoked anger on the part of the audience.", "Câu đùa của anh ta khiến khán giả tức giận.", "provoked|on the part of"], ["It seems to be + noun + that + V", "It seems to be the weather that makes me tired.", "Dường như chính thời tiết làm tôi mệt.", "it seems"], ["If one + V, one must + V", "If one wants to succeed, one must work hard.", "Nếu muốn thành công, người ta phải chăm chỉ.", "if one|one must"], ["My own opinion is that + clause", "My own opinion is that the plan is too risky.", "Theo tôi, kế hoạch này quá rủi ro.", "my own opinion"], ["As soon as + clause, + clause", "As soon as I arrived, it started to rain.", "Ngay khi tôi đến, trời bắt đầu mưa.", "as soon as"], ["The more + ..., the less + ...", "The more you worry, the less you sleep.", "Càng lo lắng, bạn càng ngủ ít.", "the more|the less"], ["S + be + identical to + that of + noun", "My phone is identical to that of my sister.", "Điện thoại của tôi giống hệt của chị tôi.", "identical to"], ["S + should not be confused with + noun", "Confidence should not be confused with arrogance.", "Không nên nhầm sự tự tin với sự kiêu ngạo.", "confused with"], ["S + amount(s) to + noun", "His excuse amounts to a lie.", "Lời bào chữa của anh ta chẳng khác gì nói dối.", "amounts to|amount to"], ["In terms of + noun, ...", "In terms of price, this hotel is the best.", "Xét về giá, khách sạn này tốt nhất.", "in terms of"], ["S + be + so + adj + that + clause", "The music was so loud that I couldn't hear.", "Nhạc to đến mức tôi không nghe được gì.", "so"], ["S + derive(s) from + noun", "Many English words derive from Latin.", "Nhiều từ tiếng Anh bắt nguồn từ tiếng La-tinh.", "derives from|derive from"], ["So much for + noun.", "So much for my plan to relax this weekend.", "Thế là xong kế hoạch nghỉ ngơi cuối tuần của tôi.", "so much for"], ["S + do(es) not jibe with + noun", "His story doesn't jibe with the facts.", "Câu chuyện của anh ta không khớp với sự thật.", "jibe"]]$j$::jsonb
)
