."], [393.4, "In the year 2020, there will be a guy named Bill."], [398.4, "Bill will be scared of heights."], [401.2, "He will hate high places."], [403.6, "In fact, he's going to avoid them at all costs."], [408.6, "Bill will engage in a lot of strange behavior to avoid heights."], [413.0, "For example, he won't go upstairs."], [417.1, "He'll always stay on the first floor."], [420.9, "One day, Bill is going to decide to join a class for people who hate heights."], [426.6, "The teacher will tell the class, I will cure you if you do what I tell you."], [431.9, "Bill will be receptive to the teacher's ideas because he's going to be tired of being afraid."], [440.6, "On the first day of the class the teacher is going to say."], [444.9, "Today we will go back to square one."], [447.8, "We will start by climbing just two stairs."], [451.2, "The next day they will climb five stairs."], [454.2, "The next day they will climb twenty."], [456.9, "As they climb the teacher is going to yell, you are strong!"], [461.4, "You can do it!"], [463.2, "Bill will internalize these messages."], [466.1, "He will feel brave."], [467.4, "He will feel strong."], [470.8, "However, other students are going to drop out of the class like flies."], [477.4, "But Bill is going to stay."], [479.8, "On the final day, Bill will watch a movie about mountain climbing."], [484.6, "The movie is going to approximate the experience of being on a mountain."], [489.7, "But Bill will feel no fear."], [493.3, "The class will work."], [496.0, "Bill will He'll no longer be afraid of heights."], [500.6, "He's going to leave immediately, and then he's going to climb Mount Everest."], [508.4, "Okay, that's all."], [510.6, "Listen to each one of these many times."], [514.4, "Especially compare them, right?"], [516.4, "Listen to each one."], [518.2, "When you talk about verb tenses, switching verb tenses in English,"], [524.4, "pay attention to, concentrate on clues."], [528.3, "Introductory words or phrases."], [530.5, "Certain phrases, certain words tell you when to switch."], [534.7, "For example, one day, one day Bill decided, right?"], [539.7, "One day was a clue."], [541.6, "It told me, ah, now it's one specific day."], [545.3, "Maybe I need to change, especially talking about the past."], [548.9, "Or eight years ago."], [551.0, "Ah, now we know it was in the past and it's finished; that tells us what to do."], [560.3, "Or “since 2003”: ah, that tells us it started in 2003 and it has continued until now, it's still happening, until now or until recently."], [573.1, "“In 2020”: that tells us it's in the future."], [577.7, "So notice those phrases in each of these versions of the story."], [583.9, "Listen to each version."], [585.6, "Many times, you will begin to learn the grammar effortlessly without studying grammar, without trying to memorize it."], [594.1, "Don't think about grammar."], [595.2, "If you think too much, your speaking will be slow."], [599.0, "If you think too much, your speaking will be unnatural."], [602.6, "You will never be fluent if you have to think about grammar for every sentence you use."], [610.7, "It's impossible."], [612.6, "You have to learn it deeply."], [614.9, "You have to internalize the grammar."], [618.7, "You have to learn it unconsciously, instinctively, effortlessly, without conscious thinking."], [626.1, "You must internalize the grammar."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.8, "Okay, welcome to the commentary for the TPR and Listen First article."], [7.5, "This is a very interesting article."], [9.2, "I'm very fascinated with TPR."], [12.1, "TPR is a fantastic technique for teaching languages."], [16.7, "It is especially great for low beginners."], [22.0, "Now, you can use it for many different levels, But if you have somebody who has zero language, zero English, zero Japanese, they want to learn the language and they know nothing."], [34.3, "TPR is a great way to start them learning."], [38.1, "In fact, I think it's the best way that I know to start them learning."], [42.2, "TPR has a lot of great research about it around it."], [46.7, "So we know from a lot of research that TPR is more effective, more powerful, successful than traditional methods, more successful than audio-lingual methods."], [60.3, "More successful than grammar analysis."], [63.0, "Not just a little bit more successful, a lot more successful."], [68.2, "TPR is very powerful."], [70.4, "If you want to learn a new language and you have zero ability."], [74.6, "Try to find a TPR program because it's a great way to learn a language."], [81.8, "TPRS stands for TPR Storytelling."], [85.6, "It's kind of the next technique that comes after TPR and TPRS, TPR Storytelling, that's what I do in our mini-story lessons, so they go together quite well."], [99.6, "But anyway, in this article, it's a research article, basically, it's kind of a casual language research article, I changed the language a little bit to make it more conversational."], [111.0, "More direct."], [112.4, "But anyway, it discusses a few different studies."], [114.4, "These studies are quite interesting."], [116.3, "There are a lot more studies."], [118.4, "When I was doing my master's thesis, I learned about some of this research."], [124.0, "Because when I got my master's in teaching English, I knew something was wrong."], [130.5, "I had already been a teacher."], [132.8, "I had been teaching English several years before my master's degree."], [138.2, "I had also tried to learn Japanese."], [141.5, "I'd tried to learn Italian."], [145.2, "I'd tried a little bit of trying to learn Spanish in the past."], [150.0, "I even had taken Mandarin."], [152.3, "I took two semesters of Mandarin Chinese in university."], [158.0, "And these methods totally failed me."], [161.2, "They did not work."], [163.7, "I took two semesters, that's almost one year."], [167.6, "Of Chinese."], [169.0, "And now I remember possibly one sentence in Chinese."], [174.0, "Maybe six words."], [175.8, "That's not good."], [178.0, "But even worse, after two semesters, I could not remember very much."], [183.4, "And I certainly could not use Chinese, and I definitely could not understand it."], [188.6, "The same happened with Spanish when I studied Japanese on my own."], [194.2, "I lived in Japan."], [195.5, "I was living in Japan for six months in Aomori."], [199.7, "Surrounded only by Japanese people."], [203.0, "Studying Japanese every day myself."], [206.5, "And yet I could not speak Japanese after six months at all."], [212.9, "I mean, not a little bit."], [214.0, "I could not chat at all in Japanese."], [216.6, "Someone said something in Japanese; unless it was super simple, like “konnichiwa”, hello, I didn't understand."], [223.6, "So for a long time I thought something is wrong with me."], [228.9, "AJ, well, you're a smart guy, but man, you're bad with languages, you're just stupid with languages, you cannot learn a language."], [238.5, "That's what I thought; I thought I had some problem."], [242.9, "But then I became an English teacher."], [246.0, "And I noticed, wow, a lot of other people have the same problem."], [250.5, "All these students are failing, not just in my classes, but in everybody's classes."], [257.1, "All these English classes."], [259.6, "The students are studying for years, one year, two years, four years, six years studying English."], [267.8, "And they still cannot have a normal average conversation."], [272.8, "They still struggle, it's still difficult."], [277.2, "And I started thinking, wow, something is wrong."], [280.6, "It's not the people, it's not the students, it's not me."], [284.5, "I don't have a brain problem with languages."], [287.6, "The problem has to be something else."], [290.9, "And I realized, after I started doing my master's degree, I started learning about a lot of this research, I realized, aha."], [299.4, "The problem is the teaching method."], [301.6, "The problem is the textbooks are the textbooks that we use."], [307.1, "That's the problem."], [308.8, "That's why so many people fail foreign languages."], [313.2, "That's why so many people hate foreign languages."], [317.1, "That's why so many students think foreign language study is painful and horrible and frustrating."], [324.6, "Writing."], [325.9, "And just like the article says, so many people."], [328.9, "Especially in America."], [330.3, "They study a foreign language a few years."], [332.7, "And they learn only to hate the language."], [335.6, "That's all they learn."], [336.7, "They never learn how to use the language or understand it well."], [340.8, "Only thing they learn is, oh man, Spanish is really difficult."], [344.3, "It's complicated."], [346.1, "And that's Spanish."], [346.9, "You know, Spanish is pretty, pretty easy actually for English speakers."], [350.5, "It's quite close to English compared to Japanese or Chinese or Korean."], [357.1, "But still, you know, I took some Spanish classes in high school and I thought, oh my God, this is so complicated."], [363.0, "All these grammar rules, the subjunctive, and oh, I don't understand it, I'm confused."], [369.8, "And then I listened to a tape in Spanish."], [371.8, "I listened to Spanish speakers."], [373.5, "I have no idea what they're saying, even if they speak slowly."], [377.3, "Even if they would speak very simply."], [380.0, "I still could not communicate."], [383.0, "It was very frustrating, but I started my master's program, I started reading this research, I became excited because I realized, number one,"], [393.1, "the old methods clearly don't work for most people."], [397.2, "Yes, a few people can succeed with traditional methods."], [400.7, "It's true, a few, but it's like five or ten percent only."], [404.9, "Not many people."], [406.0, "Most people fail with those methods."], [408.2, "So I realized the methods are the problem."], [410.8, "Even better, even more hopeful and optimistic, I found out there are successful methods."], [417.0, "There are much better methods that are, number one, they're more successful."], [422.5, "Number two, they're more enjoyable, they're more fun."], [426.0, "Number three, they teach communication, not grammar rules, not standardized tests."], [432.5, "And I started finding these different kinds of methods and studying them."], [438.2, "I was very lucky that I lived in Bangkok, Thailand for a while."], [443.8, "The article mentions the AUA Thai program."], [447.2, "A Listen First Thai language program in Bangkok."], [452.2, "At AUA, it stands for American University Alumni School."], [456.8, "It's a very respected school in Thailand."], [459.5, "They have an English program for Thai people, and they have a Thai language program."], [466.6, "Now their English program uses normal methods, I think, I don't know, really."], [470.4, "But their Thai program is special."], [472.6, "It uses a listen-first approach."], [476.5, "People learning Thai just listen to Thai for a long time."], [481.1, "Now you don't just listen."], [482.4, "Listening is not the only important thing."], [484.6, "You have to listen to something you understand."], [487.0, "And if your level is low, ooh, that's a tough job for the teacher."], [492.0, "How can I give them English, for example?"], [495.0, "How can I give them language that is simple enough for them to understand?"], [500.8, "Well, TPR uses actions to convey meaning, to show meaning."], [507.3, "That's why it's so powerful."], [509.0, "TPR does not require translation."], [511.8, "I can teach English with TPR with no translation."], [517.8, "I do not need to know the students' language."], [521.0, "I do not need to translate to Spanish or Japanese or French or anything."], [526.0, "With TPR, I use actions to show them what the words mean."], [532.4, "And I can teach someone who knows zero English using this technique."], [537.2, "And they will learn quickly, very quickly, as a matter of fact."], [542.1, "They will very quickly learn to understand the meaning of the English words."], [547.4, "And also very quickly they will learn to understand first single words, then phrases, then full sentences."], [554.3, "TPR is powerful; it is so fast, I love it."], [558.3, "I wish I could use it somehow on the internet."], [562.4, "Maybe in the future I might use video to do that, create some video TPR lessons."], [568.9, "However, the truth is, most English learners are not low beginners."], [574.6, "You have all learned in your schools."], [577.7, "Unfortunately you learned with bad methods, most of you, but still you have a good amount of vocabulary."], [584.1, "So TPR is not so necessary."], [589.0, "However, Tomoe is starting Effortless Japanese."], [592.4, "And Tomoe will use TPR."], [595.7, "Because with Japanese."], [598.2, "Most people have not studied Japanese before."], [601.4, "There are a lot of low beginners, a lot of zero level Japanese learners."], [607.1, "So she's going to use learning guides plus TPR to teach low level Japanese, starting from zero."], [616.1, "If you know no Japanese at all."], [618.6, "Nothing."], [619.9, "You can listen to her lessons and read her lesson guides and you will learn Japanese."], [625.7, "And quite quickly, I think."], [627.4, "You will start to get a good feeling for Japanese and it will not feel difficult."], [631.6, "It should feel easy."], [634.1, "Her website actually is starting this at the end of this week."], [638.3, "She will start testing it."], [640.2, "She will probably accept a few two beta test members."], [645.5, "I don't know how many."], [647.0, "I have to ask her."], [648.4, "I will be one of them."], [649.2, "Of course, I'll be one of her test students."], [651.6, "So I will begin learning Japanese with all of you."], [655.3, "And my Japanese skill is very, very low."], [657.5, "So I'm excited to learn."], [658.9, "I can finally learn something with TPR."], [661.6, "It's great."], [663.8, "So anyway, with English, however, I think low, low beginners, it's not so necessary on the internet."], [672.4, "So I focus more on TPRS, TPR storytelling."], [676.3, "Which is another excellent technique that is much more effective than traditional methods."], [683.7, "And this is not just my opinion because I like it."], [687.0, "There's a lot of research about this."], [689.4, "This is another technique I found when I was doing my master's thesis for teaching English."], [695.5, "I found out about TPRS, TPR Storytelling, and I was like, wow, this is much better."], [701.8, "The students learn vocabulary without trying to memorize word lists."], [706.7, "The students learn grammar without studying grammar rules."], [710.8, "And they learn real communication."], [713.6, "And they can tell the stories themselves."], [716.2, "They learn to really understand and communicate."], [719.3, "And that is, number one, the most important goal."], [723.8, "There's another very powerful technique which I use here in San Francisco, it's called focal skills."], [732.4, "Focal skills."], [733.6, "There are different parts to focal skills, but the best part, my favorite part is the movie technique."], [739.6, "You use movies to teach the language."], [744.2, "You don't just show the movie, that's not enough."], [747.6, "Most of you know if you just watch a movie in English, it's too fast, you can't understand it."], [752.4, "So that's not good."], [753.9, "But if a teacher shows the movie, if they show one scene of the movie, maybe two minutes."], [760.0, "They show it one time, normal speed, then they stop, they rewind."], [765.2, "Next, they show it again, but they pause every few seconds, and they explain what's happening."], [771.0, "They use simple English that you understand."], [774.1, "They might explain some new vocabulary or slang that is used in the movie."], [779.2, "They might describe what's happening in the movie; they might point to people and things and describe them."], [785.6, "And then they play the scene again."], [788.2, "And then they go back one more time; they play the same scene a third time."], [794.0, "This time they pause, they ask the student many questions."], [797.6, "Who is this guy? What is he wearing? What does he look like? What is he doing? Why is he doing that?"], [805.5, "What is going to happen next?"], [807.4, "So it becomes a conversation."], [809.4, "The teacher is asking many, many questions about the movie, and the students are answering these questions."], [814.9, "So after you watch each scene like this, three different times, the teacher then goes to the next scene."], [821.6, "It takes a long time to watch one movie, but the point is not to watch a movie."], [826.3, "The point is to learn the language."], [828.2, "And in this way, you learn real language."], [830.4, "Movies are much more real than textbooks."], [833.8, "Textbooks are fake."], [835.1, "Nobody speaks like that."], [836.4, "Don't use textbook English."], [838.5, "Movie English is much closer to real conversational English."], [845.0, "Movies are perfect textbooks."], [848.0, "Textbooks are not good."], [850.4, "Anyway, that's another different kind of technique."], [853.1, "There are many techniques."], [853.9, "Techniques, not only one effortless English, I try to use the best techniques I know that can be used on the Internet."], [863.4, "So that's what I'm doing with you, TPR storytelling."], [867.3, "Reading articles and listening to them many times."], [870.6, "Changing the point of view for the articles."], [873.8, "For the mini stories."], [875.5, "These are things that can be done easily on the Internet that you can do easily by yourself."], [880.1, "It's very cheap for you, it's very simple, and it works."], [884.7, "It works much better than a textbook."], [887.2, "If you need to find a school, some people like school, some people want to see a teacher face-to-face."], [892.2, "That's fine."], [893.6, "But try to find a school that uses TPRS, or focal skills, or TPR, or a natural approach."], [902.9, "Try to find that."], [903.8, "They all say they use the natural approach."], [906.1, "Just be careful."], [906.9, "School."], [907.4, "All these schools, they say, oh, we use the natural approach."], [910.2, "But in fact, most of them do not."], [913.3, "In fact, most of them use the same textbooks and the same methods."], [917.3, "So if you're looking for a school, be careful when you shop."], [921.5, "Ask a lot of questions."], [923.9, "All righty."], [924.3, "That's all for today's commentary."], [925.8, "It's a topic I'm quite fond of."], [928.1, "I like it a lot, of course."], [930.1, "Good luck with your English learning."], [932.0, "Just keep listening."], [933.0, "Listen into those mini stories."], [934.4, "I think the mini story lessons are the best."], [937.2, "That's why I added a new one."], [938.6, "Now you have two mini stories for each lesson."], [941.4, "Please listen to those many, many, many times and then listen to the articles, etc."], [946.5, "Okay, I'll see you next time."], [948.2, "Good luck."], [948.8, "Please enjoy your English learning."], [950.8, "Have fun."], [951.5, "Be enthusiastic."], [953.0, "Bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["foreign language", "/ˈfɒrən ˈlæŋɡwɪdʒ/", "ngoại ngữ"], ["drop like flies", "/drɒp laɪk flaɪz/", "bỏ cuộc hàng loạt"], ["dropout rate", "/ˈdrɒpaʊt reɪt/", "tỷ lệ bỏ học"], ["satisfactory", "/ˌsætɪsˈfæktəri/", "đạt yêu cầu"], ["proficiency", "/prəˈfɪʃnsi/", "sự thành thạo"], ["standardized test", "/ˈstændədaɪzd test/", "bài kiểm tra chuẩn hóa"], ["hold a conversation", "/həʊld ə ˌkɒnvəˈseɪʃn/", "duy trì cuộc trò chuyện"], ["fluent", "/ˈfluːənt/", "trôi chảy"], ["at all costs", "/ət ɔːl kɒsts/", "bằng mọi giá"], ["frustration", "/frʌˈstreɪʃn/", "sự thất vọng"], ["approach", "/əˈprəʊtʃ/", "cách tiếp cận"], ["consist of", "/kənˈsɪst ɒv/", "bao gồm"], ["drill", "/drɪl/", "bài luyện tập lặp lại"], ["communicative", "/kəˈmjuːnɪkətɪv/", "mang tính giao tiếp"], ["theoretically", "/ˌθɪəˈretɪkli/", "về mặt lý thuyết"], ["infinite", "/ˈɪnfɪnət/", "vô hạn"], ["consequently", "/ˈkɒnsɪkwəntli/", "do đó"], ["approximate", "/əˈprɒksɪmeɪt/", "gần giống với"], ["acquisition", "/ˌækwɪˈzɪʃn/", "sự tiếp thu"], ["native language", "/ˈneɪtɪv ˈlæŋɡwɪdʒ/", "tiếng mẹ đẻ"], ["receptive", "/rɪˈseptɪv/", "tiếp nhận"], ["in advance of", "/ɪn ədˈvɑːns ɒv/", "đi trước, vượt"], ["delay", "/dɪˈleɪ/", "trì hoãn"], ["comprehension", "/ˌkɒmprɪˈhenʃn/", "khả năng hiểu"], ["internalize", "/ɪnˈtɜːnəlaɪz/", "thấm sâu, tiếp thu"], ["beneficial", "/ˌbenɪˈfɪʃl/", "có lợi"], ["significantly", "/sɪɡˈnɪfɪkəntli/", "đáng kể"], ["in sum", "/ɪn sʌm/", "tóm lại"], ["supplement", "/ˈsʌplɪmənt/", "sự bổ trợ"], ["go back to square one", "/ɡəʊ bæk tə skweə wʌn/", "quay lại từ đầu"], ["extensive", "/ɪkˈstensɪv/", "nhiều, sâu rộng"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["as successful as it should be", "thành công như lẽ ra phải thế"], ["students are dropping like flies", "học sinh bỏ cuộc hàng loạt"], ["as high as 85 percent", "lên tới 85%"], ["less than satisfactory proficiency", "trình độ chưa đạt yêu cầu"], ["proficient enough to hold a conversation", "đủ thành thạo để trò chuyện"], ["will probably never become fluent", "có lẽ sẽ không bao giờ nói trôi chảy"], ["avoid the foreign language at all costs", "né tránh ngoại ngữ bằng mọi giá"], ["the lack of success", "sự thiếu thành công"], ["came into wide use", "được dùng rộng rãi"], ["pattern practice drills", "bài luyện mẫu câu"], ["it is logical to conclude that", "hợp lý khi kết luận rằng"], ["doing just that", "làm được chính điều đó"], ["TPR stands for", "TPR là viết tắt của"], ["listening first and then speaking", "nghe trước rồi mới nói"], ["far in advance of speaking", "vượt xa khả năng nói"], ["delaying speech is beneficial", "trì hoãn việc nói là có lợi"], ["focus most of your energy on listening", "dồn phần lớn sức lực vào việc nghe"], ["as long as listening remains the major focus", "miễn là nghe vẫn là trọng tâm chính"], ["go back to square one", "quay lại từ đầu"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["S + has not been as + adj + as + it should be", "The trip has not been as fun as it should be.", "Chuyến đi không vui như lẽ ra phải thế.", "as|should be"], ["S + be + as high as + number", "Prices are as high as 50 dollars.", "Giá lên tới 50 đô.", "as high as"], ["S + be + adj + enough to + V", "She is old enough to drive.", "Cô ấy đủ tuổi lái xe.", "enough to"], ["Not only will + S + V, (but) S + will also + V", "Not only will you save money, you will also save time.", "Bạn không chỉ tiết kiệm tiền mà còn tiết kiệm thời gian.", "not only"], ["That is, + clause", "He is a vegan. That is, he doesn't eat any animal products.", "Anh ấy ăn thuần chay. Nghĩa là không ăn bất kỳ sản phẩm động vật nào.", "that is"], ["This is because of + noun", "This is because of the bad weather.", "Đó là vì thời tiết xấu.", "because of"], ["S + consist(s) of + noun / V-ing", "The test consists of three parts.", "Bài kiểm tra gồm ba phần.", "consist of|consists of"], ["It is logical to conclude that + clause", "It is logical to conclude that he was tired.", "Hợp lý khi kết luận rằng anh ấy đã mệt.", "conclude"], ["A + stands for + B", "UN stands for United Nations.", "UN là viết tắt của United Nations.", "stands for"], ["S + be + delayed until + clause", "The game was delayed until the rain stopped.", "Trận đấu bị hoãn cho đến khi tạnh mưa.", "delayed until|until"], ["Only after that should + S + V", "Only after that should you sign the contract.", "Chỉ sau đó bạn mới nên ký hợp đồng.", "only after"], ["As for + noun, ...", "As for me, I prefer tea.", "Còn tôi thì thích trà hơn.", "as for"], ["..., as long as + clause", "You can go out, as long as you come back early.", "Con có thể ra ngoài, miễn là về sớm.", "as long as"], ["It is best to + V", "It is best to start early.", "Tốt nhất là bắt đầu sớm.", "it is best"]]$j$::jsonb
)
