lic."], [754.8, "q", "Who else is a full-fledged alcoholic?"], [758.7, "a", "Well, Lassiter is also a full-fledged alcoholic."], [762.7, "q", "Are they both full-fledged alcoholics?"], [766.5, "a", "Yes, they are."], [767.5, "s", "They are both full-fledged alcoholics."], [770.8, "s", "Gana and Lassiter become full-fledged alcoholics."], [773.9, "s", "But they enjoy their jobs every day now."], [778.9, "s", "Alright, now, one more time, I'm going to pause after key phrases."], [783.6, "s", "Just copy my pronunciation, say the phrase, and copy my pronunciation."], [788.6, "s", "Let's go."], [789.8, "s", "Lassiter is a meticulous person."], [795.2, "s", "Lassiter is a meticulous person."], [797.5, "s", "He loves math and accounting."], [800.2, "s", "He gets giddy about counting pennies."], [806.2, "s", "He gets giddy about counting pennies."], [812.2, "s", "Lassiter works with a guy named Gana."], [814.3, "s", "Gana hates accounting."], [817.4, "s", "He thinks it's drudgery."], [821.3, "s", "He thinks it's drudgery."], [825.4, "s", "Gana is an outlandish guy."], [830.2, "s", "Gana is an outlandish guy."], [834.2, "s", "He loves to party and drink and laugh."], [837.7, "s", "One day at work, Lassiter argues with Gana."], [841.2, "s", "He says to Gana, life doesn't revolve around parties."], [848.3, "s", "Life doesn't revolve around parties."], [850.5, "s", "Please, you need to be more careful and meticulous with your work."], [858.0, "s", "Gana laughs and he says, you are so boring, Lassiter."], [863.3, "s", "Life should be jubilant and fun always."], [869.9, "s", "Life should be jubilant and fun always."], [876.6, "s", "Then Gana takes a beer out of his desk and throws it to Lassiter."], [881.2, "s", "Drink this he says, then you'll have more fun at work."], [884.8, "s", "Lassiter drinks the beer and feels much happier."], [888.7, "s", "Work seems much more fun now."], [891.7, "s", "Finally, Lassiter says, we are friends now."], [894.7, "s", "We have good camaraderie."], [899.3, "s", "We have good camaraderie."], [907.5, "s", "Thanks, Gana."], [908.7, "s", "I'm going to drink every day at work and enjoy life for its own sake."], [916.2, "s", "And enjoy life for its own sake."], [921.0, "s", "Gana and Lassiter eventually become full-fledged alcoholics."], [930.2, "s", "Gana and Lassiter eventually become full-fledged alcoholics."], [937.6, "s", "But they enjoy their jobs."], [941.9, "s", "Okay, now please pause and try to tell all of the story yourself."], [947.6, "s", "Try to tell all of the story and use the vocabulary correctly."], [951.9, "s", "You don't need to remember every word, but do try to use the correct phrases and words."], [958.4, "s", "All right."], [958.8, "s", "See you next time."], [959.8, "s", "Bye."]]}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.2, "Hello, welcome to the Point of View mini-stories for First Battle."], [7.3, "Same story, three different versions."], [10.6, "Version number one, 25 years ago."], [16.0, "25 years ago, there was a man named Lassiter."], [20.1, "Lassiter was a meticulous person."], [22.5, "He loved counting."], [24.5, "He got giddy about counting pennies."], [27.6, "Lassiter worked with a guy named Gana."], [30.9, "Gana hated accounting."], [32.5, "He thought it was drudgery."], [35.0, "Gana was an outlandish guy who loved to party and drink and laugh."], [42.0, "One day at work, Lassiter argued with Gana."], [45.0, "He said, life doesn't revolve around parties."], [48.6, "You need to be more careful with your work."], [51.7, "Gana laughed and said, you are so boring."], [55.2, "Life should be jubilant and fun always."], [58.6, "Then Gana took a beer out of his desk and threw it to Lassiter."], [62.9, "\"Drink this,\" he said."], [64.4, "\"Then you'll have more fun at work.\""], [67.5, "Lassiter drank the beer and felt much happier."], [71.0, "Work seemed much more fun now."], [73.3, "He said, \"Gana, we are friends now."], [76.6, "We have good camaraderie."], [78.4, "Thanks."], [79.2, "I'm going to drink every day at work and enjoy life for its own sake.\""], [88.1, "Gana and Lassiter eventually became full-fledged alcoholics, but they enjoyed their jobs."], [95.2, "All right, version number two."], [98.6, "Version number two, okay?"], [101.3, "So we'll say something changed last year."], [105.3, "Last year, something happened, and Lassiter and Gana changed their personalities."], [112.6, "Their personalities changed for some reason."], [114.5, "And maybe in the past, in the far past, Lassiter was more relaxed."], [119.8, "And maybe in the far past, Gana was more serious."], [124.2, "But something happened last year."], [126.1, "We don't know what."], [126.8, "But something happened, and they changed their personalities."], [130.0, "Let's begin."], [132.4, "There's a guy named Lassiter."], [134.3, "Since last year, Lassiter has been a very meticulous person."], [140.2, "He has loved accounting."], [141.6, "He has gotten giddy about counting pennies since last year."], [149.3, "Since last year, Lassiter has worked with a guy named Gana."], [152.7, "Gana has hated accounting during that time."], [156.2, "He has thought it was drudgery."], [159.8, "During this time, Gana has been an outlandish guy who loves to party and drink and laugh."], [168.1, "One day at work, Lassiter argued with Gana."], [171.7, "He said, life doesn't revolve around parties."], [175.3, "You need to be more careful with your work."], [178.3, "Gana laughed and said, you are so boring."], [181.7, "Life should be jubilant and fun always."], [184.2, "Then Gana took a beer out of his desk and threw it to Lassiter."], [188.0, "Drink this, he said, then you'll have more fun at work."], [191.6, "Lassiter drank the beer and felt much happier."], [194.3, "Work seemed much more fun now."], [197.2, "He said, we're friends now, Gana."], [199.4, "We have good camaraderie, thanks."], [201.9, "I'm going to drink every day at work and enjoy life for its own sake."], [209.3, "Gana and Lassiter eventually became full-fledged alcoholics, but they enjoyed their lives and their jobs much more."], [217.8, "Okay, very nice."], [219.1, "Now, in this case we could change this story a little bit; maybe I'll do a number four version here."], [227.4, "We could start with, you know, since last year Lassiter has been meticulous."], [232.8, "Maybe Gana and Lassiter started to work together last year."], [236.6, "And when they met each other, they changed their personalities for some reason."], [242.4, "Or we could say Lassiter is a meticulous person."], [246.5, "We could use the present tense."], [248.2, "But then we could say, since last year, Lassiter has worked with a guy named Gana."], [253.3, "So it means his job situation changed last year and that job has continued until now."], [262.4, "Okay, so it's just a matter of meaning: how we change the verb tenses changes the meaning of the timeline, of what has happened in time."], [273.8, "Okay, anyway, let's go on to the future version now, the future version."], [279.0, "Ten years from now, there will be a guy named Lassiter."], [283.7, "Lassiter will be a meticulous person."], [286.2, "He'll love accounting."], [287.4, "He'll get giddy about counting pennies."], [290.4, "Lassiter will work with a guy named Gana."], [293.6, "Gana will hate accounting."], [295.5, "He'll think it's drudgery."], [297.3, "Gana is going to be an outlandish guy who loves to party, and drink, and laugh."], [302.6, "One day at work, Lassiter will argue with Gana."], [305.3, "He'll say, life doesn't revolve around parties."], [308.3, "You need to be more careful with your work."], [310.1, "Gana will laugh and say, you are so boring."], [314.1, "Life should be jubilant and fun always."], [316.6, "Then Gana will take a beer out of his desk and throw it to Lassiter."], [320.4, "\"Drink this,\" he'll say, \"then you'll have more fun at work.\""], [324.6, "Lassiter will drink the beer and he'll feel much happier."], [328.2, "Work will seem much more fun now."], [331.4, "He'll say, we are friends now."], [333.7, "We have good camaraderie."], [335.2, "Thanks, Gana."], [335.6, "I'm going to drink every day at work and enjoy life for its own sake."], [340.7, "Gana and Lassiter are eventually going to become full-fledged alcoholics, but they'll enjoy their jobs."], [350.4, "Okay, those are the three versions."], [352.6, "Once again, listen to the three versions."], [355.1, "Go back, listen to each one, then pause after each version and try to tell it yourself."], [362.1, "Try to use the correct verb forms and the correct vocabulary when you tell the story."], [367.7, "If you have trouble, it's okay."], [369.8, "Go back."], [370.5, "Listen again."], [371.1, "Maybe pause after every sentence and say each sentence yourself."], [377.1, "Then play one more sentence, pause again, and say that sentence."], [382.8, "So if you can't do all of the story, go sentence by sentence."], [386.7, "That's okay too."], [388.7, "And don't think too much about the grammar."], [390.8, "This is important."], [391.5, "Don't think too much about it."], [393.8, "Don't analyze it."], [395.2, "Don't try to remember all the rules, okay?"], [399.1, "Just listen, understand the meaning, and try to say it yourself."], [404.5, "Do not think about it too much, okay?"], [407.2, "See you next time."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.4, "Hello, and welcome to the commentary for First Battle."], [5.7, "Alright, let's chat a little bit about this article."], [8.7, "This article was written by me."], [11.0, "So this is a true story."], [13.5, "And I wrote this article originally for a magazine in Georgia."], [18.4, "So it was published in a magazine called Flagpole Magazine in Georgia."], [23.3, "I made the article a little bit shorter and a little simpler for Effortless English."], [29.5, "But it's basically the same article, and it's true."], [32.7, "I did belong to this group for about 10 years, I guess; I was a member of this group."], [39.6, "I joined when I went to university, to undergrad, and I went to this, I guess you would call it an activity fair, for freshmen, for new students."], [49.6, "We went and you could see all the different clubs and organizations at the university, and one of them was this group, the SCA."], [58.2, "And I thought, oh wow, this looks really interesting and strange and fun."], [62.9, "So I went to one of their meetings, and then I decided it still looked interesting."], [68.0, "So I went to the first event and that first event I describe in the beginning of this article."], [73.6, "It was a battle with about 200 people in armor and swords and it was great fun."], [80.7, "I really enjoyed it."], [82.7, "I had a really good time."], [84.6, "I remember fighting and fighting and fighting all day."], [87.8, "So after this battle, they had another battle."], [90.1, "Then they had another battle."], [92.0, "And then after that I fought just against individual people."], [96.6, "And we're using these wooden swords, but it's real fighting in the sense that it's like a martial arts competition."], [104.1, "So it's not like professional wrestling."], [107.4, "You actually do try to win."], [109.1, "And so if you hit somebody, for example, if you hit them in the head, then they die."], [115.6, "If you hit them in the chest, in the body, they die."], [119.1, "If you hit them in the arm or the leg, they lose that arm or they lose that leg."], [123.6, "They have to put it behind their back."], [125.5, "They can't use it."], [126.9, "So it's quite fun, actually."], [128.7, "And I continued going to many of these battles for many years."], [133.3, "Then finally, I went to graduate school."], [136.6, "I got busy, started teaching English, and most importantly, I started to travel."], [142.4, "And that's when I quit the group and started doing other things."], [148.3, "As I mentioned at the end of this article,"], [151.1, "The thing that I enjoyed most about this group was that it was fun."], [155.4, "It was like play."], [156.8, "It reminded me of when I was a kid, actually."], [160.0, "And we would just run around and play all the time and just have fun."], [164.0, "It was not so serious."], [165.1, "It's easy as an adult, you know, for us to become so serious all of the time."], [171.2, "This happens to me sometimes, I just work too much and I become very serious and I don't think about just having fun and playing and relaxing and being totally away from any kind of work."], [185.5, "But I think it's very important we need to do that, especially if we are in some kind of creative field or we need to be creative."], [193.7, "Well, to be creative, I think you have to play."], [197.0, "You have to play."], [197.7, "You have to enjoy life."], [199.7, "And I think what happened is that when I was younger, I was a member of this group, the SCA."], [205.0, "That was my play, my playtime, my play group."], [209.3, "And then later, I replaced the SCA with travel."], [214.6, "And travel really is now the way I play."], [217.6, "It's my way of finding new things, doing interesting things."], [222.6, "Just for its own sake."], [224.4, "So when I travel, I don't have any big serious goals usually; I just want to learn and enjoy and be surprised."], [232.4, "My favorite thing about traveling is that it surprises me."], [236.0, "I wake up in the morning and I don't know what will happen that day, right?"], [241.9, "Normally here in San Francisco, I go to work, I have a similar day each day; it's kind of a routine."], [249.5, "Most of us do that if we're working."], [252.4, "Well, I think it's important; we have to break that routine somehow."], [256.7, "One way is to join some group like the SCA."], [260.1, "You join some creative fun group and you just go out and have fun."], [265.1, "You break your work routine, right?"], [267.0, "You do things that are not so serious."], [269.9, "You do things that might be surprising or new or different."], [274.5, "Maybe you go and you learn how to dance or you go out to nightclubs or you go out with your friends somewhere, or you take a trip."], [281.9, "Or you join some interesting group."], [283.9, "But anyway, we need these things in our life, I think, so that we don't become terribly boring and dull."], [290.2, "Because if you just go to work or go to school,"], [293.3, "come home, study,"], [295.1, "go to sleep, do the same thing all the time,"], [297.6, "You become boring and dull."], [300.1, "In fact, I've had this problem recently."], [302.2, "I've been feeling quite bad recently because I feel like all I do is work."], [306.2, "I teach my class, and then I work on lessons for Effortless English, or I work on the website."], [314.0, "And then I go to bed, and then I wake up, and then I do the same thing again, and then again, and then again."], [321.8, "And it's making my brain, making my mind, kind of dull, kind of boring."], [326.1, "I'm not so interesting and that's not good."], [329.1, "So anyway, I'm trying to do some new things now."], [332.2, "I just joined a yoga club yesterday."], [336.5, "Tomoe and I are planning some travels, some trips."], [340.5, "And we're hoping by the end of the year,"], [344.0, "possibly the beginning of next year,"], [346.3, "Depending on our travel plans, we're hoping at that time that we can move to Thailand."], [351.9, "And in fact, we have plans to move to Thailand and start a school, an English school, somewhere in Thailand."], [360.0, "Probably Phuket in the south of Thailand."], [362.9, "So who knows, hopefully next year I can talk to you about the Effortless English school in Phuket, Thailand."], [371.0, "That's my hope."], [371.8, "That's my plan."], [373.2, "That's what we are hoping to do."], [375.4, "But I don't know."], [376.4, "We'll see what happens."], [377.7, "I don't know about the time right now."], [379.8, "But for now,"], [380.9, "trying to do some yoga, trying to do some fun things, and also planning some trips."], [385.9, "Tomoe and I are also talking about taking a trip to South America at the end of the year."], [390.0, "We would like to go to Ecuador and Peru, possibly Bolivia."], [395.8, "If there are any Effortless English members in those countries, we would love to visit you."], [401.5, "We would love to see you."], [402.9, "So if you're living in Peru or Ecuador or Bolivia,"], [406.8, "maybe even Chile, or anywhere in that region,"], [410.2, "then please email us, or I'll look on the member list."], [413.8, "If I can find you, maybe we'll come and visit you and chat with you."], [418.5, "Okay, well anyway, the basic message from this article is to have fun."], [424.6, "Don't always be so serious."], [427.8, "You have to enjoy your life."], [430.4, "You have to do things for their own sake, just because you like them."], [435.8, "No other reason."], [437.3, "That might be travel."], [438.7, "That might be a fun group like this."], [440.5, "It might be joining a soccer club."], [442.8, "It might be anything."], [443.9, "I don't know."], [444.2, "But I think it's a great idea, in order to be happy, to have some activities like this where you change your routine, you don't do the same thing every day, and you can just have fun and enjoy your life."], [458.4, "So please do that."], [460.1, "And you know that goes for English too."], [461.9, "Take a break from English sometimes."], [463.4, "You don't need to be so serious about English all the time."], [467.5, "It's good to be a motivated student."], [469.9, "It's good to be a serious student."], [471.5, "But sometimes you just need to have fun."], [473.5, "If you feel tired of English, no problem."], [476.1, "Just take a break."], [477.2, "Take a break."], [477.7, "Take a vacation from English."], [479.6, "Or maybe you don't want to take a vacation from English."], [482.7, "That's okay."], [483.7, "Focus only on fun things for English."], [486.6, "Just find some fun movies that you enjoy."], [489.1, "Find some funny TV shows and focus on those."], [493.1, "Learn from those."], [494.6, "Find an interesting fun book or magazine or blog or website and just learn from those."], [501.1, "Because you don't always have to be so serious."], [504.3, "Serious is good."], [505.5, "It's okay."], [507.0, "It's good to be serious a lot of the time, but you need a break sometimes."], [510.5, "So please, give yourself a break."], [512.9, "Okay, I'll see you next time, bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["howl", "/haʊl/", "tiếng gào, tru"], ["opposing", "/əˈpəʊzɪŋ/", "đối địch, phía bên kia"], ["thud", "/θʌd/", "đập thình thịch"], ["shield", "/ʃiːld/", "cái khiên"], ["in unison", "/ɪn ˈjuːnɪsn/", "đồng thanh, cùng lúc"], ["pound", "/paʊnd/", "đập mạnh"], ["grip", "/ɡrɪp/", "nắm chặt"], ["brace", "/breɪs/", "tì, chống"], ["giddy", "/ˈɡɪdi/", "phấn khích, choáng váng"], ["grin", "/ɡrɪn/", "cười toe toét"], ["wiry", "/ˈwaɪəri/", "gầy mà rắn chắc"], ["clad in", "/klæd ɪn/", "mặc, khoác"], ["stride (strode)", "/straɪd/ /strəʊd/", "sải bước"], ["insult", "/ˈɪnsʌlt/", "lời lăng mạ"], ["cowardly", "/ˈkaʊədli/", "hèn nhát"], ["goosebumps", "/ˈɡuːsbʌmps/", "nổi da gà"], ["advance", "/ədˈvɑːns/", "tiến lên"], ["awe", "/ɔː/", "sự kinh ngạc, kính sợ"], ["anachronism", "/əˈnækrənɪzəm/", "điều lỗi thời, lệch thời đại"], ["oddball", "/ˈɒdbɔːl/", "người lập dị"], ["medieval", "/ˌmediˈiːvl/", "thuộc thời Trung cổ"], ["armor", "/ˈɑːmə/", "áo giáp"], ["outlandish", "/aʊtˈlændɪʃ/", "kỳ quặc"], ["history buff", "/ˈhɪstri bʌf/", "người mê lịch sử"], ["misfit", "/ˈmɪsfɪt/", "người lạc loài"], ["succumb to", "/səˈkʌm tuː/", "khuất phục trước"], ["drudgery", "/ˈdrʌdʒəri/", "công việc tẻ nhạt, cực nhọc"], ["revolve around", "/rɪˈvɒlv əˈraʊnd/", "xoay quanh"], ["centerpiece", "/ˈsentəpiːs/", "tâm điểm"], ["patchwork", "/ˈpætʃwɜːk/", "sự chắp vá, nhiều mảnh ghép"], ["calligraphy", "/kəˈlɪɡrəfi/", "thư pháp"], ["archery", "/ˈɑːtʃəri/", "bắn cung"], ["full-fledged", "/ˌfʊl ˈfledʒd/", "hoàn chỉnh, thực thụ"], ["persona", "/pəˈsəʊnə/", "nhân dạng, vai"], ["meticulous", "/məˈtɪkjələs/", "tỉ mỉ"], ["eccentricity", "/ˌeksenˈtrɪsəti/", "sự lập dị"], ["camaraderie", "/ˌkæməˈrɑːdəri/", "tình bạn bè, đồng đội"], ["jubilant", "/ˈdʒuːbɪlənt/", "hân hoan"], ["defiance", "/dɪˈfaɪəns/", "sự thách thức, bất tuân"], ["tedium", "/ˈtiːdiəm/", "sự tẻ nhạt"], ["nurture", "/ˈnɜːtʃə/", "nuôi dưỡng"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["Hearts pounded.", "Tim đập thình thịch."], ["A wild grin broke upon my face.", "Một nụ cười điên cuồng bừng lên trên mặt tôi."], ["threw insults against them", "tuôn ra lời lăng mạ họ"], ["eyes wide with awe", "mắt mở to kinh ngạc"], ["muscles tense as steel", "cơ bắp căng như thép"], ["none of this was real", "chẳng có gì là thật"], ["refuse to succumb to the drudgery of being normal", "không chịu khuất phục trước sự tẻ nhạt của việc sống bình thường"], ["loved every minute", "yêu từng phút"], ["small by today's standards", "nhỏ so với tiêu chuẩn ngày nay"], ["is held annually", "được tổ chức hằng năm"], ["As the example implies", "Như ví dụ cho thấy"], ["is further divided into", "lại được chia nhỏ thành"], ["make a full-time living", "sống hoàn toàn bằng nghề"], ["I felt I'd been transported back in time", "tôi cảm thấy như được đưa ngược về quá khứ"], ["an exercise in living history", "một cách sống lại lịch sử"], ["a refusal to surrender to tedium", "sự từ chối đầu hàng sự tẻ nhạt"], ["for its own sake", "vì chính nó"], ["Play is not an escape. It is a celebration.", "Vui chơi không phải là trốn chạy. Đó là sự tôn vinh."], ["for the sake of our happiness", "vì hạnh phúc của chúng ta"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["I turned to see + O + V-ing/adj", "I turned to see my friend waving at me.", "Tôi quay sang và thấy bạn tôi đang vẫy tay.", "turned to see"], ["S + clad in + clothing", "A man clad in black walked in.", "Một người đàn ông mặc đồ đen bước vào.", "clad in"], ["adj + with + noun (Eyes wide with awe)", "Her face was red with anger.", "Mặt cô ấy đỏ bừng vì giận.", "with"], ["almost forgetting that + clause", "We laughed all night, almost forgetting that we had work tomorrow.", "Chúng tôi cười cả đêm, gần như quên rằng mai phải đi làm.", "almost forgetting"], ["S + refuse(s) to + V", "She refuses to give up.", "Cô ấy không chịu bỏ cuộc.", "refuse to"], ["S + revolves around + noun", "His life revolves around his kids.", "Cuộc sống của anh ấy xoay quanh các con.", "revolves around"], ["small/big by today's standards", "The phone was cheap by today's standards.", "Chiếc điện thoại rẻ so với tiêu chuẩn ngày nay.", "by today's standards"], ["As + noun + implies, ...", "As the name implies, the cafe is very quiet.", "Như cái tên cho thấy, quán cà phê rất yên tĩnh.", "implies"], ["Since I + V2, S + has/have + V3", "Since I moved here, the city has changed a lot.", "Từ khi tôi chuyển đến, thành phố đã thay đổi nhiều.", "since i"], ["At times, S + V", "At times, I feel lonely.", "Đôi lúc tôi thấy cô đơn.", "at times"], ["I am convinced that + clause", "I am convinced that he is telling the truth.", "Tôi tin chắc rằng anh ấy đang nói thật.", "convinced that"], ["for the sake of + noun", "They stayed together for the sake of their children.", "Họ ở bên nhau vì các con.", "for the sake of"]]$j$::jsonb
)
