  $j$[[0.7, "Okay, welcome to the Point of View mini-stories for Neo Bedouins."], [8.6, "So same story as the mini-story, but we're going to change the time frame."], [13.8, "We're going to start with in 1968, the year I was born."], [20.0, "Okay, here we go."], [21.8, "In 1968, there was a hip guy named Andy."], [26.9, "Andy was nomadic."], [28.0, "He could never stay in one place."], [31.6, "He loved to roam from country to country, place to place."], [36.1, "But every summer, he always stayed in San Francisco."], [40.2, "When he was in the city, his favorite hangout was the venerable Caffe Trieste."], [46.4, "The cafe used to be the place where San Francisco's famous writers hung out."], [51.4, "It was the epicenter of the San Francisco arts movement."], [55.7, "One day, Andy emerged from the cafe and he crossed paths with an old friend named Leo."], [63.4, "His friend said, I'm leaving San Francisco."], [66.6, "I'm striking out on my own to see the world."], [70.2, "Andy asked him, where are you going first?"], [73.3, "Leo said, I'm going to Vietnam."], [76.3, "It's a very beautiful place in the summer."], [79.6, "Two weeks later, Andy was reading the newspaper and saw a story."], [83.8, "The story said that Leo had been killed in Vietnam."], [89.8, "It figures, said Andy."], [92.0, "Vietnam is a very dangerous and insecure place."], [95.2, "What an idiot!"], [99.0, "Alrighty, so that was in 1968, right?"], [102.6, "In the past, in the past."], [105.6, "Next, let's begin with since 2000, since the year 2000."], [112.2, "Here we go."], [115.7, "There's a guy named Andy."], [118.6, "Since 2000, Andy has been nomadic."], [123.0, "He hasn't been able to stay in one place."], [126.2, "He has loved to roam from country to country and place to place."], [130.9, "But every summer, he has always stayed in San Francisco."], [135.8, "When he's been in the city, his favorite hangout has always been the venerable Caffe Trieste."], [141.8, "The cafe used to be the place where San Francisco's famous writers hung out."], [148.3, "It was the epicenter of the San Francisco arts movement."], [153.8, "One day, Andy emerged from the cafe and crossed paths with an old friend named Leo."], [160.3, "His friend said, I'm leaving San Francisco."], [163.6, "I'm striking out on my own to see the world."], [166.1, "Andy asked him, where are you going first?"], [170.4, "Leo said, I'm going to Iraq."], [172.7, "It's very beautiful in the summer."], [175.2, "Two weeks later, Andy read the newspaper and saw a story."], [179.2, "The story said that Leo had been killed in Iraq."], [184.1, "It figures, said Andy."], [186.4, "Iraq is a very dangerous place and it's insecure."], [190.5, "What an idiot."], [193.7, "Okay, great."], [195.5, "Alright, next one."], [197.4, "Let's go to the future."], [199.4, "We'll say next year."], [202.3, "Okay, here's my little story idea for next year."], [205.6, "There'll be a guy named Andy."], [208.1, "He'll be a hip guy."], [210.4, "Andy'll be nomadic."], [213.1, "He'll never be able to stay in one place."], [216.3, "He'll love to roam from country to country and place to place."], [219.9, "But every summer, he'll always stay in San Francisco."], [226.3, "When he's in the city, his favorite hangout will be the venerable Caffe Trieste."], [233.2, "Now, the cafe used to be the place where San Francisco's famous writers hung out."], [238.4, "It was the epicenter of the San Francisco arts movement."], [242.8, "Now, in the future,"], [244.2, "one day,"], [245.5, "Andy will emerge from the cafe, and he'll cross paths with an old friend named Leo."], [250.8, "His friend will say, I'm leaving San Francisco."], [254.0, "I'm striking out on my own to see the world."], [257.9, "And Andy will ask him, where are you going first?"], [260.5, "And Leo will say, I'm going to Iraq."], [263.4, "It's very beautiful in the summer."], [266.2, "Two weeks later, Andy will be reading the newspaper and he'll see a story."], [270.8, "The story will say that Leo was killed in Iraq."], [274.7, "It figures, Andy will say."], [277.8, "Iraq is a very dangerous and insecure place."], [280.9, "What an idiot."], [282.8, "Okay, that is all of the Point of View mini-stories for this lesson, Neo Bedouins."], [290.2, "Now, when you listen to Point of View lessons, just relax, okay?"], [295.8, "Don't worry about getting the grammar perfect."], [299.8, "It doesn't need to be perfect, okay?"], [302.2, "It takes time."], [304.2, "Listen again and again and again to the point of view mini-stories."], [309.2, "Listen to the first mini-story lesson."], [311.7, "Listen to all the lessons."], [313.3, "Relax."], [314.2, "You will start to improve your grammar automatically if you listen carefully."], [320.4, "It's okay if you make a mistake."], [322.1, "It's okay if you pause and try to tell the story, but you can't remember the grammar exactly."], [328.6, "Don't worry."], [329.6, "Don't worry."], [330.0, "It's okay."], [330.4, "Okay, just keep listening, listening, listening, listening very carefully."], [335.4, "Notice the different sounds."], [337.6, "Notice how the verbs change."], [339.6, "Notice how the vocabulary changes sometimes."], [342.7, "Just notice and listen carefully."], [345.1, "Then, if you can, pause after each version."], [349.8, "Try to tell the story using the phrase, in 1968."], [354.8, "Then tell it again, since 2000."], [356.7, "Then tell it again, next year."], [360.6, "Don't worry if you make some mistakes, it's okay."], [363.4, "Okay?"], [364.3, "Relax."], [365.1, "Alright."], [365.8, "See you next time."], [366.6, "Bye-bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.4, "Okay, welcome to the commentary for the Neo Bedouins article."], [5.7, "This is an exciting article."], [6.9, "I really like this article."], [8.3, "I saw it on the front page of the San Francisco newspaper."], [13.4, "which is called the San Francisco Chronicle,"], [16.2, "this week, a couple days ago."], [18.1, "And when I saw it and read the article, I thought, wow, this is me."], [23.1, "This is what I'm doing with Effortless English, right?"], [26.3, "I don't have an office for Effortless English."], [29.1, "In fact, I go to coffee shops here in San Francisco often."], [33.9, "And I think about the website."], [35.4, "I write down my ideas."], [37.8, "Sometimes I bring my laptop."], [39.8, "Although usually I do this in my apartment, it's actually recording, because I need a more private space to record lessons."], [48.6, "But anyway, I write the lessons in the coffee shops quite often."], [52.0, "And in the coffee shops, I always see many, many people with laptop computers."], [57.8, "And often, I will hear people having little meetings about their internet company and discussing different issues, designing their websites."], [66.6, "It's very exciting, actually, to be here in San Francisco at this time."], [73.3, "especially being involved with an Internet business,"], [77.9, "with Internet teaching."], [80.2, "Because really, in America, this is the epicenter of computer technology, of IT, Internet technology."], [90.8, "It's all right here."], [93.1, "It's happening here most of all."], [95.2, "Silicon Valley."], [97.0, "You've probably heard of Silicon Valley."], [99.6, "Silicon Valley is the place in California where there are many, many computer companies."], [107.2, "Apple Computer."], [108.5, "Hewitt Packard."], [109.9, "A lot of Japanese computer companies have offices there."], [114.0, "But Silicon Valley is near San Francisco."], [116.6, "It's a short drive from here."], [119.6, "In fact, it's between San Francisco and San Jose."], [123.7, "From San Francisco, you drive to Silicon Valley or take a train."], [128.0, "Maybe, I don't know, 30 minutes."], [129.9, "Something like that, 30, 40 minutes, not far."], [132.6, "So San Francisco and Silicon Valley, really one area."], [136.0, "And this is where all the innovation is happening in the United States with computer industry and especially the Internet."], [145.1, "So it's quite exciting to be here, involved in that."], [147.4, "It's kind of a really great energy, a lot of new and interesting things happening."], [153.2, "Lots of creative, innovative people."], [156.7, "A lot of flourishing."], [158.9, "Growing, succeeding internet companies."], [161.4, "I mean, Google is based here, for example, Yahoo as well."], [167.2, "So anyway, it's fantastic."], [168.4, "It's a great place to be if you are involved in the computer industry or if you're involved in the Internet in any way."], [177.3, "Another thing about this article that I liked a lot, that I said, wow, that's me, is the part about the nomadic tribes being nomadic."], [187.9, "Traveling around."], [190.3, "That's another reason I have chosen to teach with the Internet."], [195.7, "Now, I believe that teaching with the Internet and also learning with the Internet is just amazing."], [201.8, "It's so flexible."], [204.2, "You can be nomadic and still have a business."], [208.3, "You can be nomadic and still have all your English learning materials, right?"], [214.0, "With your computer, the internet, and your little iPod, that's all you need."], [218.8, "You can go anywhere."], [220.2, "You can travel to a beach in Thailand, but still study English, right?"], [226.1, "You've got your iPod, that's all you need."], [227.9, "There's internet connections everywhere."], [229.4, "So, it's very simple and it's so much more flexible than in the past."], [237.0, "It's the same for me with Effortless English."], [239.4, "I can do Effortless English from anywhere."], [242.8, "So, if I want to travel to Mexico, I can go to Mexico and continue to work on the website."], [248.8, "I can travel to Thailand."], [250.5, "I can live in Thailand and still do the website, still build Effortless English."], [255.5, "I can move around, I can be nomadic, and I love that because I love traveling."], [261.2, "The reason I love teaching English is that it connects me to people all over the world."], [268.9, "I just love going to different places in the world."], [271.7, "I love meeting new people."], [273.8, "I love seeing and learning about new cultures."], [278.0, "It's just fantastic."], [279.5, "So it's really exciting to me."], [281.1, "I have a lot of emotion about this topic, because this is why I'm doing it."], [287.0, "This is why I'm doing Effortless English."], [290.0, "It's just really exciting."], [291.4, "It's an exciting time."], [293.7, "Another key point in the article is about this idea of self-employment."], [300.8, "It's not just nomadic employment."], [303.6, "It's self-employment."], [304.6, "It means you are your own boss."], [308.1, "And this idea that the job market is insecure."], [312.3, "There's a lot of insecurity now in my father's generation."], [318.4, "He worked for IBM over 20 years, one company."], [322.0, "That was normal for him."], [325.5, "But here now in my generation and younger in the United States, that is not normal."], [331.7, "Almost nobody works for the same company for 20 years."], [335.8, "It doesn't happen."], [337.3, "They get fired."], [338.5, "They get laid off."], [340.5, "Because older workers are expensive, and the company wants to save money, so they cut their older workers."], [347.0, "There's just no job security in America anymore."], [350.8, "It's a reality."], [353.5, "Now, for me, I don't mind."], [355.0, "My dad probably doesn't like that."], [357.1, "Maybe older people think that's a bad thing."], [359.6, "But there's a good side to it, and the good side is in this article, and that is we can be more independent."], [366.2, "Now we have the ability."], [369.0, "With computer technology, with the Internet."], [371.4, "With a lot of things, to be our own boss."], [374.9, "We can start our own companies."], [377.2, "And we can be freelancers, meaning we do some work and we sell it to other people."], [382.4, "Whoever will buy it."], [384.2, "Writers and photographers do this a lot."], [386.3, "But now we can do this with many, many different things."], [389.0, "And that's exciting."], [390.4, "Why is it exciting to me?"], [392.1, "Well, to be honest, I don't like bosses."], [393.9, "In fact, I hate working for other people."], [398.0, "I hate having a boss tell me how to teach or what book I must use or what method I must follow."], [406.9, "Yeah, it's not good for me because I don't listen to them and that gets me in trouble."], [412.6, "It got me in trouble in Thailand, in fact."], [415.1, "I have a strong idea about how I should teach and what I'm good at and what is my best teaching style and how to make English learning more fun, more interesting and more effective."], [431.2, "And unfortunately, or maybe fortunately, I don't know, but anyway, those ideas go against traditional English teaching."], [439.1, "I don't like textbooks, for example."], [441.3, "I refuse to use them."], [442.9, "I won't use them."], [445.0, "I certainly won't spend all my time in class teaching from a textbook."], [451.1, "I don't like grammar analysis because it does not work."], [454.6, "It just does not work for most people."], [457.4, "It fails most students."], [459.5, "So I don't like doing things I know are failures."], [462.7, "I don't like doing things I know will not help the students."], [466.6, "So I disobey."], [468.4, "I don't follow my boss's advice."], [470.9, "I don't listen to my bosses."], [472.0, "And, you know, they don't like that sometimes."], [475.9, "So after I had a lot of trouble in Thailand."], [478.9, "Because I was doing my own method, not using their methods."], [484.3, "Somebody told me, actually somebody on Tom Peters' blog told me, AJ, you have to start your own business."], [491.2, "Your personality and your ideas, they're too different."], [494.9, "You will never be happy working for another person."], [499.0, "You must be an entrepreneur."], [500.3, "You must start your own business."], [502.4, "And that's when I started really thinking about, you know, I need to do this myself."], [507.6, "I want to teach the way I feel is best."], [512.3, "The way I'm the best at teaching, the best style for me."], [516.2, "And what I think is best for students."], [518.7, "That is always what I want to follow, not some rule from a company, not some principal or bosses rule."], [526.5, "I want to do what I think is best."], [528.3, "So, the only way to do that, really, is to start your own business."], [533.4, "And it doesn't matter, even if you're not a teacher."], [535.8, "If you're a doctor."], [538.4, "And you want to treat your patients the best, you can treat them."], [543.2, "You have your very strong ideas how to do that."], [546.2, "Well, you have to have your own business, your own medical practice, your own medical business, to do that."], [552.2, "If you work in a hospital, you probably have bosses telling you what to do."], [556.1, "If you're a business person, maybe you have strong ideas about what is right and what is wrong."], [561.8, "If you have your own business, you can follow those."], [565.0, "But if you work for someone else, well, they might want you to do things you think are not good, or not ethical, right, not moral."], [573.2, "Maybe you think, oh, I don't want to lie to my customers, I have to tell them the truth."], [579.3, "If I make a mistake or something is bad, I have to tell them the truth."], [584.4, "But maybe your company says, no, no, no, you have to lie to them."], [588.8, "Right?"], [589.0, "Some people, in fact, a lot of people don't like that."], [592.5, "Well, the only way to follow your own principles is to have your own business."], [597.3, "And so anyway, that's the long answer to why I love self-employment, why I think it's great."], [605.0, "Unfortunately, right now, I am a part-time Bedouin."], [609.0, "In fact, a lot of these Bedouins you see in the coffee shops, a lot of them are part-time with a startup, with a new company."], [616.2, "You know, you have no money."], [618.3, "You have very little money."], [620.9, "So usually you have to work another job at the same time while you build your company."], [627.3, "So I'm doing that right now."], [628.9, "I'm building Effortless English slowly, but I don't have enough money to do it all the time."], [634.8, "I can't do Effortless English full time right now."], [639.1, "I did not borrow money to start this website."], [642.6, "I do not want to borrow money."], [644.6, "I don't want to bank controlling or owning the website."], [648.8, "So I want it to be mine so I can do it my way."], [652.3, "So right now I teach, I'm teaching classes here in San Francisco to students in San Francisco and I'm doing the website part time."], [660.5, "I'm a part time Bedouin."], [661.7, "In the future, I hope to do it full time."], [664.7, "And that's what a lot of these internet companies are doing, and you see these people in the coffee shops, many of them are part-time."], [671.0, "Some of them are full-time, maybe they're making enough to survive."], [674.3, "And they're trying to build their business."], [678.2, "And they're trying to do it in a very cheap way without borrowing money from a bank, or at least borrowing a very small amount."], [687.7, "And that's really exciting if you think about it, because anybody."], [692.0, "Any Effortless English member could start their own business."], [697.4, "You can start your own business on the internet."], [700.9, "Get a laptop computer for, I don't know, Apples are about a thousand dollars."], [706.9, "I think Windows would be cheaper."], [709.8, "So you get a laptop computer."], [712.1, "I mean that's expensive but compared to the past it's very, very cheap."], [717.4, "In the past you had to borrow ten thousand dollars."], [720.2, "One hundred thousand dollars."], [721.6, "Well now a thousand dollars you can use a credit card if necessary or you can work and save your money."], [727.4, "You can get a laptop computer."], [730.0, "You can get internet connections for free in some coffee shops."], [734.9, "I know in America you can."], [736.8, "In Thailand, yes, I could do that sometimes."], [740.8, "In Bangkok I found free internet access."], [745.4, "Or you can find it very cheap somewhere."], [749.2, "And you know, and you get a cell phone for your phone."], [751.8, "That's all."], [752.6, "You have your business."], [753.5, "You're ready to go."], [755.0, "Now you have to, you know, of course find a website."], [758.0, "You can usually, you can start a Yahoo store or Google has internet business programs to help you create your website."], [768.8, "And they're also quite cheap."], [770.4, "So there's an amazing opportunity to start your own business if you want to."], [776.2, "So I encourage you, if you have thought about it in the past, maybe I should start my own business."], [780.2, "Well, do it!"], [781.4, "Do it!"], [782.3, "Try it."], [782.9, "You can do it part-time."], [784.5, "Keep your normal job."], [786.0, "Start your website."], [788.3, "It's okay if you don't know what to do."], [791.6, "When I started Effortless English, I didn't know anything."], [795.3, "I didn't know anything about business."], [797.8, "I still don't, really."], [799.1, "I just tried things."], [801.6, "I started it."], [802.7, "I tried something."], [803.9, "Sometimes it worked."], [805.3, "It was successful."], [806.4, "Sometimes it failed."], [808.1, "If it failed, I got rid of it."], [810.0, "I threw it away."], [810.8, "And I tried something else."], [812.3, "That's how I am developing Effortless English."], [814.3, "I just try things, and try things, and try things."], [817.0, "Some things are good, and I keep them."], [819.2, "Some things are bad."], [820.5, "I throw them away."], [822.3, "That's all you do."], [823.4, "That's it."], [824.0, "That's the key to starting your own business."], [825.5, "Just start it cheap, try things, keep the stuff that works, get rid of stuff that fails."], [832.7, "Keep doing that again and again, every year, every month."], [836.0, "Every week, every day."], [837.7, "And you will build a business."], [839.7, "So good luck."], [840.2, "I hope that more people will do this because it's very exciting."], [843.7, "And it feels so good to have something yourself."], [847.7, "It's yours."], [848.7, "You are building it."], [849.9, "You are responsible."], [852.7, "That's huge."], [853.7, "It's really important."], [854.5, "And it's a good feeling."], [857.1, "I love Effortless English."], [858.5, "I don't care if I make a lot of money or not, but I really love being responsible for it."], [864.4, "I love that it's mine, that I'm building it together with learners."], [870.6, "No other boss."], [871.6, "Nobody telling us what to do."], [873.4, "It's fantastic."], [874.3, "It really is great."], [876.0, "All right."], [876.4, "So I encourage you, become a Neo Nomad."], [879.4, "Become a Neo Bedouin yourself."], [882.1, "All right."], [882.5, "See you next time."], [883.3, "Bye-bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
